-- import-3.8.4-reef.sql - met une base reef-moteur deja en 3.8.3 au niveau de la 3.8.4 : les tableaux des articles de demonstration deviennent de vrais tableaux, trois textes d'aide du back office sont remis a jour.
--
-- Les articles de demonstration verses par scripts/moteur-import.mjs avant la
-- 3.8.4 gardaient leurs tableaux Markdown en paragraphes ("| a | b |"), dans
-- l'editeur comme sur le site. Chaque article encore dans cet etat recoit son
-- texte relu du fichier de src/data/posts, ses tableaux en bloc "Tableau" de
-- l'editeur. Un article dont le tableau a deja ete refait (ou retire) n'est
-- pas touche.
--
--   node scripts/base-3.4.0.mjs --remote reef-moteur --sql import-3.8.4-reef.sql              (le plan, rien n'est ecrit)
--   node scripts/base-3.4.0.mjs --remote reef-moteur --sql import-3.8.4-reef.sql --appliquer
--
-- IDEMPOTENT : un second passage ne change rien. Aucun DELETE, aucun DROP.
-- Textes convertis par scripts/markdown-en-texte-riche.mjs (la conversion de
-- l'import).

-- 1. TEXTES D'AIDE. Sujets et Auteurs se choisissent par leur nom depuis la
-- 3.8.3 : leur description ne demande plus d'ajouter un identifiant. Le champ
-- de la lettre externe dit que la lettre integree passe avant lui.
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _emdash_collections WHERE slug = 'sujets' AND description = 'Les sujets du blog : chacun a sa page, sa couleur et sa description. Pour ranger un billet dans un nouveau sujet, ajoutez aussi son identifiant aux choix du champ « Sujet » des Articles (Types de contenu).' | la description de la collection sujets dit comment choisir une nouvelle entree par son nom
UPDATE _emdash_collections SET description = 'Les sujets du blog : chacun a sa page, sa couleur et sa description. Un nouveau sujet se choisit aussitôt, par son nom, dans le champ « Sujet » d''un article.'
  WHERE slug = 'sujets' AND description = 'Les sujets du blog : chacun a sa page, sa couleur et sa description. Pour ranger un billet dans un nouveau sujet, ajoutez aussi son identifiant aux choix du champ « Sujet » des Articles (Types de contenu).';
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _emdash_collections WHERE slug = 'auteurs' AND description = 'Les personnes qui signent les billets : chacune a sa page. Pour signer un billet d''un nouvel auteur, ajoutez aussi son identifiant aux choix du champ « Auteur » des Articles (Types de contenu).' | la description de la collection auteurs dit comment choisir une nouvelle entree par son nom
UPDATE _emdash_collections SET description = 'Les personnes qui signent les billets : chacune a sa page. Une nouvelle personne se choisit aussitôt, par son nom, dans le champ « Auteur » d''un article.'
  WHERE slug = 'auteurs' AND description = 'Les personnes qui signent les billets : chacune a sa page. Pour signer un billet d''un nouvel auteur, ajoutez aussi son identifiant aux choix du champ « Auteur » des Articles (Types de contenu).';
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _emdash_fields WHERE collection_id = (SELECT id FROM _emdash_collections WHERE slug = 'site') AND slug = 'form_newsletter' AND label = 'Adresse d''un service externe qui reçoit les inscriptions à la lettre (vide : le formulaire reste une démonstration et n''envoie rien)' | le libelle du champ de la lettre externe dit que la lettre integree passe avant
UPDATE _emdash_fields SET label = 'Adresse d''un service externe qui reçoit les inscriptions à la lettre, si vous n''utilisez pas la lettre intégrée (vide, et sans courriels branchés : le formulaire n''envoie rien)'
  WHERE collection_id = (SELECT id FROM _emdash_collections WHERE slug = 'site') AND slug = 'form_newsletter' AND label = 'Adresse d''un service externe qui reçoit les inscriptions à la lettre (vide : le formulaire reste une démonstration et n''envoie rien)';


-- 2. TABLEAUX DES ARTICLES DE DEMONSTRATION.
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « A performance budget that survives contact with a client » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"k1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k0","text":"Every studio says it cares about performance. Almost none of them can tell you, before the project starts, what number would make them refuse a feature. That gap is the whole problem: without a threshold agreed in advance, \"fast\" is a taste, and taste loses every argument against a marketing department.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2","text":"We started writing performance budgets into the statement of work in 2023. They have failed twice, which taught us more than the times they worked.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4","text":"The four numbers","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6","text":"A budget with nine metrics is a wish list. Ours has four, and each one exists because it protects a different person.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t0","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r1","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8","text":"Metric","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ka","text":"Target","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kc","text":"Protects","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ke","text":"Largest Contentful Paint","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kg","text":"2.0 s at p75[^p75]","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ki","text":"The reader deciding whether to stay","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r9","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ca","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk","text":"Interaction to Next Paint","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cb","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"km","text":"200 ms at p75","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cc","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ko","text":"Anyone who taps a menu on a cheap phone","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"rd","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ce","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kq","text":"Cumulative Layout Shift","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cf","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ks","text":"0.05","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cg","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ku","text":"The reader who just lost their place","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"rh","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ci","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kw","text":"Page weight, article template","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cj","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ky","text":"180 KB compressed","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ck","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10","text":"The client, from us","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12","text":"The last row is the one clients ask about, and it is the one we care about most. The three Core Web Vitals are outcomes: they move for reasons you do not fully control, including the CDN, the visitor’s network and the phone in their pocket. Page weight is an input. It is the number the team actually sets, every day, with every decision, and it is the only one you can check without deploying anything.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14","text":"[^p75]: p75 means the 75th percentile of real visits: three out of four readers get that experience or better. Chrome’s field data aggregates it over a rolling 28 day window, which is also why a fix you shipped last Tuesday does not show up in the report yet.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k17","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16","text":"The device is part of the number","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k19","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18","text":"A target without a device is not a target. \"LCP under two seconds\" measured on a MacBook on office fibre is a statement about our office, not about the site.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1b","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1a","text":"We measure on a mid range Android phone from three years ago, on a throttled connection, and we say so in writing. In practice that means CPU throttling around 4x and a network profile close to slow 4G, which is what Lighthouse’s mobile preset simulates by default. The first time a client sees their own site under those conditions, the meeting changes character entirely. Nobody needs convincing after that, and no slide deck has ever done the same job.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1d","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1c","text":"Writing it down where the build can read it","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1e","text":"A budget nobody automates is a budget that expires quietly around week six. Ours lives in a file:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k1g","language":"json","code":"[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"/*\",\n    \"resourceSizes\": [\n      { \"resourceType\": \"document\", \"budget\": 20 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"script\", \"budget\": 40 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"stylesheet\", \"budget\": 25 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"font\", \"budget\": 95 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"total\", \"budget\": 400 }\n    ],\n    \"resourceCounts\": [\n      { \"resourceType\": \"third-party\", \"budget\": 4 }\n    ],\n    \"timings\": [\n      { \"metric\": \"largest-contentful-paint\", \"budget\": 2000 },\n      { \"metric\": \"cumulative-layout-shift\", \"budget\": 0.05 }\n    ]\n  }\n]"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1i","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1h","text":"Sizes are in kibibytes, timings in milliseconds, and the file is understood directly by the Lighthouse CLI:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k1j","language":"bash","code":"npx lighthouse \"https://staging.example.com/journal/first-post/\" \\\n  --budget-path=./perf/budget.json \\\n  --form-factor=mobile \\\n  --output=json --output-path=./perf/report.json \\\n  --chrome-flags=\"--headless=new\""},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1l","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1k","text":"The run happens on every pull request that touches templates, and the job fails on a budget violation rather than on a score. Scores are a weighted composite that changes between Lighthouse versions; a budget is a promise with a unit attached. When the number moves, the pull request tells you which resource type moved it, and that conversation takes two minutes instead of an afternoon.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1n","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1m","text":"The clause that does the actual work","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1p","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1o","text":"Automation catches regressions. It does not answer the political question, which always arrives around week nine and always sounds reasonable. The contract answers it:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1s","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1q","text":"The budget is a fixed quantity, not a target.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1r","text":" Nobody is asked to be under it on average.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1v","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1t","text":"New weight requires equivalent weight to leave.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1u","text":" A 90 KB video header is fine if 90 KB of something else goes, and the client picks what.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k1y","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1w","text":"Third parties count as ours.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k1x","text":" An analytics tag, a chat widget and a consent manager are three of the four allowed third parties, so the fourth is a decision, not an accident.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k21","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k1z","text":"A violation is a release blocker, not a ticket.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k20","text":" The site ships slow or it ships later. There is no third option and no backlog to hide it in.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k23","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k22","text":"The point of writing this down is not legal leverage. We have never invoked it in anger. Its real function is that it moves the argument from week nine, when the budget is spent and everyone is tired, to week zero, when it is an abstract discussion between adults who still like each other.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k25","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k24","text":"Where our budgets failed","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k27","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k26","text":"Twice, and both times for the same reason: the site left our hands.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k29","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k28","text":"The tags nobody was watching","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2b","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2a","text":"The first failure was a client whose marketing team added six tags through a tag manager the month after launch. Page weight tripled. Nothing in our process was even watching, because our automation ran on pull requests, and there were no pull requests. Now the same Lighthouse run happens weekly against production on a schedule, and the report goes to the client’s inbox, not ours.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2d","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2c","text":"The four megabyte photograph","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2e","text":"The second was a content problem dressed as an engineering problem. An editor uploaded a 4.2 MB photograph through the CMS, which resized it politely for display and served the original anyway on the article page, because the template asked for the source. That is our bug, not theirs, and the fix was a pipeline that makes the wrong thing impossible: uploads are transcoded to AVIF and WebP with explicit dimensions, and the template cannot reference an original file at all.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2h","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2g","text":"Both failures share a shape worth naming. A budget protects the code you write. It does nothing about the content and the tags that arrive later, which is where the weight actually accumulates over a site’s life. If you write only one automated check after launch, do not make it a synthetic test of your own template. Make it a weekly run against the live page, on the phone your readers really use, sent to the person who can say no.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2j","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2i","text":"What it costs","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2l","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2k","text":"An afternoon at the start of the project, a CI job of about thirty lines, and the discipline to let a build fail on a Friday. In exchange you get a site that is still fast at the end of the engagement, which is the only measurement anyone outside the team ever makes.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'a-type-scale-you-can-defend' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « A type scale you can defend » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"k2p","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2m","text":"Ask a designer where their type scale came from and you usually get a ratio: a major third, a perfect fourth, the golden ratio if the project has ambitions. Ask what the fourth step is ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2n","text":"for","marks":["em"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k2o","text":" and the room goes quiet.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2r","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2q","text":"A ratio is a way of generating candidates. It is not a design decision, and it cannot be, because it does not know what is on your page. The scales that survive contact with real content are the ones where every step has a job, and where the person who chose them can say what breaks if you delete one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2t","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2s","text":"Five steps, five jobs","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k2v","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2u","text":"This is the scale for this journal. Five sizes, and one of them is used exactly once per page.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"tl","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"rm","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cn","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2w","text":"Step","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"co","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k2y","text":"Job","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cp","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k30","text":"Mobile","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cq","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k32","text":"Desktop","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cr","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k34","text":"Line height","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"rs","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ct","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k36","text":"Display","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cu","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k38","text":"The article title, once","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cv","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3a","text":"32 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cw","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3c","text":"56 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cx","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3e","text":"1.05","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"ry","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"cz","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3g","text":"Section","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c10","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3i","text":"h2, the reader’s map","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c11","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3k","text":"24 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c12","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3m","text":"30 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c13","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3o","text":"1.2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r14","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c15","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3q","text":"Sub","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c16","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3s","text":"h3 and h4, rare","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c17","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3u","text":"20 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c18","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3w","text":"22 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c19","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k3y","text":"1.3","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r1a","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k40","text":"Body","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k42","text":"Everything you actually read","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k44","text":"18 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k46","text":"19 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k48","text":"1.6","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r1g","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1h","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4a","text":"Meta","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1i","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4c","text":"Dates, captions, footnotes","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4e","text":"15 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4g","text":"15 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4i","text":"1.5","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4l","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4k","text":"Two things in that table are worth arguing about, so let me argue for them.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4n","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4m","text":"Body text starts at 18 px, not 16. The 16 px default is a browser convention from an era of 96 dpi desktop monitors, and on a phone held at arm’s length it is small. Every time we have raised body size on a client site, time on page went up and nobody wrote in to complain that the text was too large.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4p","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4o","text":"Meta text does not shrink further on mobile. Small text is where accessibility quietly fails, and 15 px is our floor. If something needs to be smaller than the floor to fit, the layout is wrong, not the type.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4r","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4q","text":"The ratio is a starting point you are allowed to break","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4t","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4s","text":"A 1.25 ratio from an 18 px base gives 18, 22.5, 28, 35, 44. Neat, and useless at the top: 44 px is not a title, it is a large heading, and the page has no moment of arrival. So we break the ratio at the display step and jump to 56, because that step has a different job from the rest of the scale. It is not \"one size up from a section heading\", it is the thing that tells you the article has begun.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4v","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4u","text":"Down at the small end we round to whole pixels rather than carrying the ratio’s decimals. Sub pixel type sizes are a real thing browsers can render, and they are also a way of pretending that 22.4 px and 22 px are different design decisions. They are not.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4x","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4w","text":"Steps that scale by ratio: body, sub, section.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k4z","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k4y","text":"Steps that are set by hand: display (it is a poster) and meta (it is a floor).","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k51","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k50","text":"Steps we deleted: two of them, because nothing on any template used them, and a scale nobody uses is a scale that produces inconsistency the first time someone needs a size that is not there.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k53","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k52","text":"Fluid, without the magic","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k57","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k54","text":"Between the two columns of that table sits ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k55","text":"clamp()","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k56","text":", and it is worth writing so a human can read it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k58","language":"css","code":":root {\n  /* 32px at 320px viewport, 56px at 1240px, linear between. */\n  --step-display: clamp(2rem, 1.478rem + 2.609vw, 3.5rem);\n  --step-section: clamp(1.5rem, 1.37rem + 0.652vw, 1.875rem);\n  --step-body:    clamp(1.125rem, 1.103rem + 0.109vw, 1.1875rem);\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5a","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k59","text":"The middle value is not a magic number, it is a line through two points. The slope is the size difference divided by the viewport difference, and the intercept is what is left when you subtract the slope’s contribution at the small end:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k5b","code":"slope     = (56 - 32) / (1240 - 320) = 0.02609  ->  2.609vw\nintercept = 32 - (0.02609 x 320)     = 23.65px  ->  1.478rem"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5d","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k5c","text":"Two rules that keep it honest","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5t","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k5n","_type":"link","href":"https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/resize-text.html"},{"_key":"k5q","_type":"link","href":"https://utopia.fyi"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k5e","text":"Write the intercept in ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5f","text":"rem","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5g","text":", never in ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5h","text":"px","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5i","text":", so the whole expression still responds when a reader raises their browser’s default font size; a clamp built only from ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5j","text":"px","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5k","text":" and ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5l","text":"vw","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5m","text":" ignores that preference and quietly fails ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5o","text":"WCAG 1.4.4","marks":["k5n"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5p","text":". And never let the fluid range be the whole design: below 320 and above 1240, the value locks, which is exactly what you want on a 1900 px monitor where a title that keeps growing becomes a billboard. If you would rather not do the arithmetic, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5r","text":"Utopia","marks":["k5q"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k5s","text":" generates the same expressions from the same four inputs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5v","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k5u","text":"The three words the arguments are actually about","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5x","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k5w","text":"<dl> <dt>Measure</dt> <dd>The length of a line of text, counted in characters. 60 to 75 is the comfortable range for continuous prose; below 45 the eye jumps too often, above 85 it loses the start of the next line. Set it in ch and it follows the font.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k5z","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k5y","text":"  <dt>Leading</dt> <dd>The space between lines, set as unitless line-height so it multiplies the element’s own size. It should grow as the measure grows and shrink as the type gets bigger: 1.6 for body text, 1.05 for a display title.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k61","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k60","text":"  <dt>Tracking</dt> <dd>Uniform letter spacing. Large type nearly always needs a little negative tracking, small type and uppercase need a little positive. It is the adjustment people reach for first and need least.</dd> </dl>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k63","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k62","text":"In CSS that is four declarations, and they do more for readability than any font choice:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k64","language":"css","code":".prose {\n  max-inline-size: 68ch;\n  font-size: var(--step-body);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n  text-wrap: pretty;\n}\n\n.prose h1 {\n  font-size: var(--step-display);\n  line-height: 1.05;\n  letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n  text-wrap: balance;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k69","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k65","text":"text-wrap: balance","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k66","text":" evens out the lines of a short heading so you never get five words and then one. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k67","text":"text-wrap: pretty","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k68","text":" does the humbler job on body copy, preventing the single word orphan at the end of a paragraph. Both are hints rather than guarantees, and both cost nothing when unsupported.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6b","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6a","text":"Testing it on the two widths that matter","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6d","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6c","text":"A scale that only looks right in the design file is not a scale. Ours gets checked on exactly two viewports, both with real content: 320 px, because that is still the narrowest phone in the field data, and 1440 px, because that is where a long title has room to embarrass you.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6e","text":"The tests are boring on purpose:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6h","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6g","text":"Does the longest real article title fit in three lines at 320 px without breaking a word?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6j","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6i","text":"At 1440 px, is the measure still under 75 characters, or did the container quietly grow?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6l","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6k","text":"Does the page still make sense at 200% browser zoom, which is the same test as asking whether any size is locked in px?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6n","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6m","text":"Do two adjacent steps look different enough that a reader can tell a section from a subsection without counting pixels?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6p","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6o","text":"The question that kills scales","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k6u","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k6r","_type":"link","href":"/blog/the-real-cost-of-a-web-font/"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6q","text":"Question four is the one that does it. If you cannot tell the difference, you do not have two steps, you have one step and a rounding error, and the fix is to delete one rather than to add contrast somewhere else. The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k6s","text":"cost of a second typeface","marks":["k6r"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k6t","text":" is a separate discussion, but a scale that needs one to be legible was never a scale in the first place.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'a-type-scale-you-can-defend' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'dark-mode-is-a-content-problem' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Dark mode is a content problem » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"k6y","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6v","text":"Every dark mode estimate I have ever written was wrong in the same direction. The colours take an afternoon. The month goes to the things that are not colours: a client logo with a baked in white background, a chart library that hardcodes ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k6w","text":"#333","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k6x","text":", a photograph of a product on seamless white that now punches a hole through the page, and a brand coral that looked confident on paper and looks radioactive at nine at night.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k70","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k6z","text":"Dark mode is not a theme. It is a second edition of the content.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k72","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k71","text":"The palette really is the easy part","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k74","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k73","text":"Two CSS features have removed most of the plumbing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k76","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k75","text":"First, tell the browser what you support, so that form controls, scrollbars, spellcheck underlines and the default canvas stop fighting you:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k77","language":"css","code":":root {\n  color-scheme: light dark;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k79","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k78","text":"Then let one declaration carry both values:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k7a","language":"css","code":":root {\n  --surface: light-dark(oklch(99% 0.005 250), oklch(21% 0.02 250));\n  --text: light-dark(oklch(28% 0.02 250), oklch(92% 0.01 250));\n  --border: light-dark(oklch(90% 0.01 250), oklch(32% 0.02 250));\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7b","text":"light-dark()","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7c","text":" picks a value based on the used colour scheme, and it only works if ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7d","text":"color-scheme","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7e","text":" is set, which is a nice piece of API design: the feature refuses to work until you have made the declaration that fixes the native widgets anyway.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7h","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7g","text":"The reason to write those in OKLCH rather than hex is that the first number is perceived lightness. Inverting a hex palette by flipping numbers produces colours that are mathematically opposite and visually wrong, because sRGB has no idea how bright a human thinks something looks. In OKLCH you can say \"same hue, same chroma, lightness 21 instead of 99\" and get a result that reads as the same colour in a different room.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7j","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7i","text":"One correction that surprises people: in dark mode, pure white text on pure black is worse, not better. It vibrates, it smears for readers with astigmatism, and it makes long articles tiring. Our defaults sit around 92% lightness on 21%, which is high contrast without the glare.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7l","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7k","text":"What the palette does not control","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7n","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7m","text":"Here is the list that actually consumes the budget.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7s","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7o","text":"Photographs on white.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7p","text":" A product shot on seamless white becomes a rectangle of daylight in the middle of a dark page. Either you get cutouts with transparency, or you accept a small compromise: ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7q","text":"filter: brightness(0.92) contrast(1.02)","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7r","text":" takes the edge off without visibly changing the product.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k7v","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7t","text":"Screenshots.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7u","text":" A screenshot of a light interface is unfixable by filter, and inverting it is a lie. We either shoot the interface twice, or we place it on a light card that is intentionally light in both modes, framed so it reads as a quotation.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k80","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k7w","text":"Charts and diagrams.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7x","text":" Anything with hardcoded stroke colours needs a real dark variant. SVG is the only sane format here, because it can inherit ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7y","text":"currentColor","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k7z","text":" and stop being an image problem entirely.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k83","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k81","text":"Code samples.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k82","text":" Two themes, switched with the rest of the page. A light code block on a dark article is the first thing a developer notices and the last thing they forgive.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k86","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k84","text":"Embedded third parties.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k85","text":" Video players, maps, comment widgets and consent banners all have their own opinion. Some take a parameter. Some do not. Budget for the ones that do not.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k89","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k87","text":"The brand colour.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k88","text":" This one deserves its own section.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k8b","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8a","text":"The brand colour will need a sibling","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k8d","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8c","text":"A single accent value cannot serve both modes. Here is the coral from our own tokens, measured against the two surfaces:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t1m","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r1n","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8e","text":"Colour","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8g","text":"On light surface","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1q","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8i","text":"On dark surface","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r1r","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1s","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8k","text":"Coral 55","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8m","text":"4.7:1, passes for body text","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8o","text":"2.1:1, fails everything","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r1v","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1w","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8q","text":"Coral 72","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8s","text":"2.3:1, fails","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c1y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8u","text":"6.4:1, passes comfortably","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k8z","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k8w","text":"There is no single value in that column that works twice. The honest fix is two tokens with one semantic name: ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k8x","text":"--accent","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k8y","text":" resolves to Coral 55 in light and Coral 72 in dark, and the markup never knows which one it got. WCAG asks for 4.5:1 on body text and 3:1 on large text and on the visible parts of interface components, and a link colour that only passes in one mode is a colour that fails half your readers.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k93","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k90","text":"If a token needs a ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k91","text":"dark:","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k92","text":" override in the markup, the token is wrong. Fix the layer that defines the colour, not the eleven places that use it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k95","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k94","text":"The flash, and the one script we allow","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k97","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k96","text":"A theme that respects a stored preference has a genuine problem: the server does not know the preference, so the first paint can be wrong. The fix is a small blocking script in the head, and it is one of the few places where a blocking script is correct:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k98","language":"astro","code":"---\n// src/components/ThemeInit.astro - runs before first paint, on purpose.\n---\n\n<script is:inline>\n  const stored = localStorage.getItem(\"theme\");\n  const dark = stored\n    ? stored === \"dark\"\n    : window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\").matches;\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle(\"dark\", dark);\n</script>"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9a","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k99","text":"Two traps in seven lines","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9i","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9b","text":"Two details cost us a bug each. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9c","text":"is:inline","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9d","text":" is required, otherwise the bundler moves the script and it no longer runs before paint. And if the site uses view transitions, the swap replaces the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9e","text":"<html>","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9f","text":" element’s attributes with the server rendered ones, so the class has to be re-applied on ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9g","text":"astro:after-swap","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k9h","text":" or the page flashes back to light on the second navigation.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9k","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9j","text":"While you are in the head, ship the matching browser chrome:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k9l","language":"html","code":"<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#fbfaf8\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#131a22\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\">"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9n","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9m","text":"That is the address bar on mobile Safari and Chrome. Getting it wrong is the difference between a site that looks designed and one that looks like a document someone printed into a browser.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9p","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9o","text":"What we tell clients now","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9r","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9q","text":"Dark mode is quoted as a content deliverable, not a styling task, and the quote includes three lines they can act on: a set of images with transparent backgrounds, a decision about the brand colour in dark contexts, and a named person who will look at the ten most visited pages in both modes before launch.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9t","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9s","text":"That last one is not a joke. Every dark mode bug we have shipped was on a page nobody thought to look at twice: a legal page with an inherited table style, a 404 with a background image, an email template that is not even part of the site. The palette is a system, and systems are good at pages you designed. Content is not a system, and it will be waiting for you on the page you forgot.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'dark-mode-is-a-content-problem' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'measuring-what-the-reader-feels' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Load time measured on the reader's phone, not in the lab » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"k9v","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9u","text":"Last autumn a client’s site scored 98 in Lighthouse and had a Largest Contentful Paint of 1.4 seconds on our test runs. The same site, in Chrome’s field data, sat at 3.9 seconds at the 75th percentile. Both numbers were correct. They were answers to different questions, and only one of the questions was about the client’s readers.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9x","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9w","text":"That gap is the reason we now install field measurement on every site we ship, before launch, as part of the build rather than as an afterthought.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k9z","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k9y","text":"Two instruments, two jobs","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t1z","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r20","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c22","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"s21","text":"","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c23","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ka0","text":"Lab (synthetic)","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c24","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ka2","text":"Field (real users)","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r25","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c26","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ka4","text":"Who is measured","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c27","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ka6","text":"One scripted visit","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c28","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ka8","text":"Everyone, on their own device","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r29","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2a","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kaa","text":"Network","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kac","text":"Simulated, consistent","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kae","text":"Whatever they have","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r2d","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kag","text":"Best at","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kai","text":"Catching regressions, comparing two builds","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kak","text":"Telling you what is actually happening","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r2h","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2i","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kam","text":"Blind to","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kao","text":"Caches, consent banners, logged in states, geography","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kaq","text":"Anything nobody visited yet","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r2l","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2m","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kas","text":"Available","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2n","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kau","text":"Before launch","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kaw","text":"After launch, with a delay","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kaz","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kay","text":"The mistake is not using one of them. The mistake is believing that a good number from the first one is a claim about the second. Lab data is a controlled experiment: change one thing, see what moves. Field data is an observation of reality, and reality includes the reader who opened your article on a train, on a four year old phone, behind a consent banner, with a battery saver throttling their CPU.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kb1","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kb0","text":"The three metrics worth collecting","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kb3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kb2","text":"Core Web Vitals are three numbers because three is roughly the number of independent things a reader can notice.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kb6","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kb4","text":"LCP","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kb5","text":" answers \"did the main thing appear\". Under 2.5 seconds at p75 is the published threshold; we target 2.0 to leave headroom.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kb9","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kb7","text":"INP","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kb8","text":" answers \"did the page respond when I touched it\". It replaced First Input Delay in March 2024 and it is much harder to fake, because it looks at every interaction of the visit rather than just the first one. Under 200 ms.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kbc","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kba","text":"CLS","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbb","text":" answers \"did the page move while I was reading\". Under 0.1, and the honest target is 0.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kbe","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kbd","text":"We collect nothing else in the first pass. Extra metrics are a way of avoiding the conclusion the first three already gave you.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kbg","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kbf","text":"The smallest honest setup","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kbl","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"kbi","_type":"link","href":"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kbh","text":"No analytics vendor, no tag manager, one endpoint of our own. The whole client side is about twenty lines, using the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbj","text":"web-vitals","marks":["kbi"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbk","text":" attribution build, which tells you not only that something was slow but which element was responsible:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kbm","language":"js","code":"import { onCLS, onINP, onLCP } from \"web-vitals/attribution\";\n\nconst queue = [];\n\nfunction record(metric) {\n  const a = metric.attribution;\n  queue.push({\n    name: metric.name,\n    // CLS is unitless, so store it scaled to keep the payload integer only.\n    value: Math.round(metric.name === \"CLS\" ? metric.value * 1000 : metric.value),\n    rating: metric.rating,\n    path: location.pathname,\n    culprit: a.interactionTarget ?? a.largestShiftTarget ?? a.element ?? null,\n    connection: navigator.connection?.effectiveType ?? null,\n  });\n}\n\nonLCP(record);\nonINP(record);\nonCLS(record);\n\naddEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", () => {\n  if (document.visibilityState !== \"hidden\" || queue.length === 0) return;\n  navigator.sendBeacon(\"/api/vitals\", JSON.stringify(queue.splice(0)));\n});"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kbo","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kbn","text":"Four deliberate choices","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kbq","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kbp","text":"Four decisions in there are deliberate.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kc3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kbr","text":"sendBeacon","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbs","text":" rather than ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbt","text":"fetch","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbu","text":", because it survives the page being closed and does not delay navigation. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbv","text":"visibilitychange","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbw","text":" rather than ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbx","text":"unload","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kby","text":", because ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kbz","text":"unload","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kc0","text":" is unreliable on mobile and disables the back forward cache, which would slow down the very readers we are trying to help.[^order] The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kc1","text":"culprit","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kc2","text":" field, because \"INP was 480 ms\" starts an investigation and \"INP was 480 ms on the topic filter button\" ends one. And a sample rate, which is not in the snippet: on a site with real traffic we send from a random slice of sessions, because a hundred percent of visits is a lot of rows to learn nothing extra from.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kc7","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kc4","text":"[^order]: Ordering matters here. The web-vitals library registers its own ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kc5","text":"visibilitychange","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kc6","text":" listener when it is imported, and finalises pending values there. Since listeners run in registration order, importing the library before adding the flush listener is what guarantees the queue is full when the beacon leaves.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kc9","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kc8","text":"The server side is a handler that validates the shape, drops anything with an unknown metric name, and appends a row. Ours writes to a SQLite file and a small query aggregates the p75 per template per week. There is no dashboard product in this stack, and after two years there has been no moment where we wished for one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcb","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kca","text":"---","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcd","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kcc","text":"When lab and field disagree, the field is right","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcf","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kce","text":"Back to the client with the 1.4 second lab score and the 3.9 second field number. The attribution data made the investigation short.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kch","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kcg","text":"The LCP element in the field was the hero image, and its breakdown showed almost all the time in resource load delay rather than in the download itself. In other words the browser knew what to fetch and could not start. The cause was a consent management script loaded synchronously in the head, which took 600 ms to arrive, then wrote inline styles that hid the hero until a decision was made. Our lab runs never saw it: our test profile had already consented, and the script short circuited.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcl","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kci","text":"The second contributor was less dramatic and more common: eleven percent of the client’s visits came in on an effective connection type of ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kcj","text":"3g","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kck","text":", from a region that was not on anyone’s list of important markets and turned out to be their second largest source of orders. The p75 of the whole audience was being set by an audience nobody had looked at.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcn","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kcm","text":"We moved the consent script to a deferred load with a reserved space for its banner, preloaded the hero, and served AVIF at three widths. Field LCP at p75 went from 3.9 to 2.1 seconds over the following four weeks, which is the lag inherent to a 28 day rolling window rather than a slow fix.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcp","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kco","text":"Two checks that cost nothing","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kcq","text":"Before writing any code, spend five minutes with the public field data for the origin. If the site has enough traffic, Chrome already collected it:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kcs","language":"bash","code":"curl -s \"https://chromeuxreport.googleapis.com/v1/records:queryRecord?key=$CRUX_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ''{\"origin\":\"https://example.com\",\"formFactor\":\"PHONE\"}'' \\\n  | jq ''.record.metrics | to_entries[] | {(.key): .value.percentiles.p75}''"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcx","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"kcu","_type":"link","href":"/blog/a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact/"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kct","text":"And keep the lab test in continuous integration, aimed at the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kcv","text":"performance budget","marks":["kcu"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kcw","text":" rather than at a score. The two instruments do different jobs: the lab tells you that this pull request made things worse, in a comparison you control. The field tells you whether the site is any good, in the only comparison that pays.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kcz","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kcy","text":"If you can only have one, take the field data. It is less convenient, it arrives late, it cannot be run on a branch, and it is the only one that has ever changed a client’s mind.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'measuring-what-the-reader-feels' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'pricing-a-redesign-without-guessing' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Pricing a redesign without guessing » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kd1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kd0","text":"There is a trap in hourly billing that took me four years to see. The better you get, the less you earn for the same work. You learn the stack, you build the tooling, you stop making the mistake you made in 2019, and the reward is an invoice that goes down. Meanwhile the client, who does not care how long the site took, is paying for your inexperience at exactly the moment you stopped having any.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kd3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kd2","text":"Hours are a unit of cost. Clients buy outcomes. Any pricing model that measures the first and sells it as the second will eventually feel unfair to somebody, usually both parties on the same project.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kd5","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kd4","text":"Three prices, one project","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kd7","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kd6","text":"We stopped sending one number in 2022. Every proposal now contains three, and they are not three sizes of the same thing: they are three different projects that solve the same problem with different amounts of ambition.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t2p","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r2q","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2s","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"s2r","text":"","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kd8","text":"Refit","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kda","text":"Rebuild","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdc","text":"Platform","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r2w","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kde","text":"What it is","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdg","text":"Existing structure, new front end","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c2z","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdi","text":"New structure, new content model, new front end","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c30","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdk","text":"Rebuild plus editorial tooling and a design system","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r31","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c32","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdm","text":"Pages designed","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c33","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdo","text":"Up to 6 templates","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c34","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdq","text":"Up to 12 templates","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c35","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kds","text":"Templates plus a component library","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r36","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c37","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdu","text":"Content","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c38","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdw","text":"Migrated as is","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c39","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kdy","text":"Restructured with the client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3a","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ke0","text":"Restructured, plus a workflow for the team","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r3b","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ke2","text":"Typical duration","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ke4","text":"4 to 6 weeks","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ke6","text":"8 to 12 weeks","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ke8","text":"14 weeks and up","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r3g","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3h","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kea","text":"Band","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3i","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kec","text":"6k to 9k","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kee","text":"12k to 18k","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"keg","text":"25k and up","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kej","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kei","text":"Three effects follow, and I did not predict any of them correctly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kel","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kek","text":"The first is that the conversation changes from \"yes or no\" to \"which one\", which is a far better conversation to be in. The second is that clients pick the middle option most of the time, which is well documented and slightly embarrassing to rely on, so we make sure the middle option is genuinely the one we would recommend. The third is the useful one: clients who choose the cheapest option do so knowing what they are not getting, and they stop asking for it in week seven, because it is written down as belonging to a different price.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ken","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kem","text":"A single quote invites a single objection: the number. Three quotes invite a decision, and a decision is a conversation you can actually help with.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kep","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"keo","text":"What we put in writing about revisions","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ker","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"keq","text":"Unlimited revisions is not generosity, it is an unpriced option that the client did not ask for and cannot value. What we write instead is short:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"keu","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kes","text":"Two rounds of consolidated feedback per deliverable.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ket","text":" Consolidated means one document from the named decider, not five emails from four people.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kex","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kev","text":"A round is a set of changes within the agreed direction.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kew","text":" Changing the direction is not a round, it is a new deliverable, and we will say so on the call rather than in the invoice.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kf0","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"key","text":"Additional rounds are quoted before they happen","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kez","text":", at a stated day rate, and they never happen by surprise.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kf3","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kf1","text":"Silence past ten working days closes the round.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kf2","text":" Not as a punishment: because a project that pauses for a month costs us the slot we held for it.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kf5","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kf4","text":"The fourth line is the one that has done the most work. Projects do not usually die from disagreement, they die from drift, and drift is expensive in a way nobody puts on an invoice.[^rate]","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kf7","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kf6","text":"[^rate]: The arithmetic that convinced me: a fixed price of 9,000 delivered in 70 hours is an effective rate of about 128 an hour. The same project, quoted hourly at 90, is worth 6,300 and takes the same skill. Fixed pricing pays you for knowing how, which is the only thing a client is actually buying.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kf9","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kf8","text":"---","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfb","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfa","text":"The two clauses that saved the most projects","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfe","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfc","text":"The content deadline clause.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kfd","text":" Copy and images are due on a date, that date is in the schedule with a named owner, and a missed content date moves the launch date by the same number of days. It sounds harsh written down and it has never once caused friction, because it is agreed at week zero when everyone is optimistic and reasonable. Without it, the studio absorbs the delay invisibly, holds the team, and then gets asked why the site launched late.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfh","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kff","text":"The pause clause.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kfg","text":" If a project stops for more than three weeks for reasons on the client’s side, restarting costs a stated fee, and the schedule is renegotiated rather than resumed. This is not a penalty, it is an honest description of what happens: we sold that time to someone else, the context has to be rebuilt, and the person who knew the codebase best is now half way into another project. Naming the cost in advance turns an awkward apology into a line item.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfj","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfi","text":"Neither clause has ever been invoked in anger. Both have changed behaviour, which is what a good clause does: it is not there to be used, it is there to be read.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfl","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfk","text":"When hourly is still the right answer","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfn","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfm","text":"Fixed pricing needs a fixed thing to price. There are three cases where we still bill time, and pretending otherwise would be dishonest: ongoing maintenance, where the work is genuinely unpredictable and the relationship is long; discovery, where the deliverable is the definition of the project itself and cannot be scoped before it exists; and emergency work, where the client wants someone available rather than someone efficient. In each of those the client is buying availability or exploration, not an outcome, and hours are the right unit for both. The mistake is not hourly billing. The mistake is hourly billing a project whose shape you already know, because you are then charging for the least valuable thing you bring, which is your time, instead of the most valuable, which is that you have done this eleven times before and know which four decisions will matter.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfp","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfo","text":"What to do on Monday","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfq","text":"If you want to change one thing, change the number of numbers. Take the next proposal you were going to send with a single price, and split it into a smaller version you would be happy to deliver and a larger one you would be proud of. Write two sentences under each explaining who it is right for. Send all three.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kft","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfs","text":"The worst outcome is that the client picks the small one, and you have a project at a price you set, with a scope you wrote, that ends on a date you chose. That is not a bad Monday.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'pricing-a-redesign-without-guessing' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'the-real-cost-of-a-web-font' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « The real cost of a web font » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kfv","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfu","text":"A client asked last month whether we could add a second typeface to their site. The licence was already paid, so as far as they were concerned the answer was free. It is a fair assumption and it is wrong, and explaining why turned into the note I wish someone had handed me years ago.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfw","text":"A web font is billed in four currencies: bytes, requests, one reflow, and a design decision you will make whether or not you notice.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kfz","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kfy","text":"Bytes, measured properly","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kg1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kg0","text":"Start with the format table, because half of the confusion lives here.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t3l","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r3m","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3n","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kg2","text":"What you serve","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kg4","text":"One Latin text weight","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kg6","text":"Worth knowing","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r3q","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3r","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kg8","text":"WOFF2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3s","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kga","text":"18 to 26 KB","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgc","text":"Brotli compressed, supported everywhere that matters","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r3u","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kge","text":"WOFF","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3w","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgg","text":"28 to 40 KB","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgi","text":"Only for browsers older than your CMS","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r3y","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c3z","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgk","text":"TTF or OTF","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c40","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgm","text":"90 to 160 KB","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c41","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgo","text":"The file the foundry sent you. Never ship it","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r42","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c43","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgq","text":"Variable, one axis, Latin subset","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c44","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgs","text":"35 to 60 KB","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c45","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgu","text":"The interesting case, below","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kgx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgw","text":"Those are ranges from our own builds, not marketing figures. A serif with a large character set lands at the top of each range, a geometric sans with tight kerning tables at the bottom.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kgz","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kgy","text":"The number that matters is not any single row. It is the total, because fonts are render blocking in the sense that counts: text either waits for them or gets swapped, and both cost something.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kh1","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kh0","text":"Variable is not automatically cheaper","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kh3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kh2","text":"This is the assumption I hear most often and it deserves a straight answer. A variable font packs every weight between its extremes into one file, plus the interpolation data to move between them. That file is bigger than one static weight and smaller than five.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kh5","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kh4","text":"The crossover is around three:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kh8","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kh6","text":"Two weights","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kh7","text":" (regular, bold): two static files win, usually by 15 to 20 KB.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"khb","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kh9","text":"Three weights","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kha","text":": roughly a tie. Pick based on whether you want optical flexibility later.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"khe","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"khc","text":"Four or more","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khd","text":", or any use of a weight that is not on the design’s list: variable wins, and it keeps winning as the design grows.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"khk","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"khf","text":"There is a second argument for variable that has nothing to do with size. With a weight axis you can set ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khg","text":"font-weight: 560","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khh","text":" on a heading and stop pretending your design only ever wanted semibold. With optical size (","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khi","text":"opsz","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khj","text":"), the face adjusts its own contrast and spacing between 14 px body text and a 72 px title, which is the thing metal type did automatically and digital type spent thirty years forgetting.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"khm","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"khl","text":"Subsetting removes less than you hope","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"khq","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"khn","text":"Subsetting means shipping only the glyphs you need. The tooling is ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kho","text":"fonttools","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khp","text":", and the command is unglamorous:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"khr","language":"bash","code":"pyftsubset SourceSerif4-Variable.ttf \\\n  --output-file=source-serif-latin.woff2 \\\n  --flavor=woff2 \\\n  --layout-features=\"kern,liga,onum,tnum,frac\" \\\n  --unicodes=\"U+0000-00FF,U+0131,U+0152-0153,U+2000-206F,U+2122\""},{"_type":"block","_key":"ki1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"khs","text":"Two warnings from experience. First, the savings are smaller than the marketing suggests for a Latin only face, because a Latin subset is most of the file already; the dramatic numbers you see quoted come from cutting Cyrillic and Greek out of a pan European font. Second, be careful with ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kht","text":"--layout-features","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khu","text":". Drop ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khv","text":"kern","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khw","text":" and your headings fall apart. Drop ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khx","text":"liga","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khy","text":" and some faces lose the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"khz","text":"fi","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ki0","text":" you were counting on. And if the site is multilingual, remember that French needs guillemets and the œ ligature, which are outside the plain ASCII range and quietly disappear if you subset by memory instead of by content.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ki3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ki2","text":"The correct move is to declare the subset in CSS as well, so the browser can skip a download it does not need on a given page:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"ki4","language":"css","code":"@font-face {\n  font-family: \"Source Serif Var\";\n  src: url(\"/fonts/source-serif-latin.woff2\") format(\"woff2\");\n  font-weight: 200 900;\n  font-display: swap;\n  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+2000-206F, U+2122;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ki6","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ki5","text":"The fallback nobody designed","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ki8","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ki7","text":"Here is the expensive part, and it costs no bytes at all.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kia","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ki9","text":"<dl> <dt>FOIT, flash of invisible text</dt> <dd>The browser hides the text while the font loads. Nothing is readable, the layout is stable, and the reader stares at an empty column. This is what font-display: block gives you.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kic","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kib","text":"  <dt>FOUT, flash of unstyled text</dt> <dd>The fallback renders immediately, then the web font replaces it. Readable at once, but the page moves when the swap happens. This is font-display: swap.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kie","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kid","text":"  <dt>Layout shift on swap</dt> <dd>The measurable cost of FOUT: the fallback and the web font have different metrics, so lines rewrap and everything below jumps. It lands in Cumulative Layout Shift and it is entirely avoidable.</dd> </dl>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kig","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kif","text":"Avoidable, because CSS can force a system font to imitate the metrics of the one still downloading:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kih","language":"css","code":"@font-face {\n  font-family: \"Source Serif fallback\";\n  src: local(\"Georgia\"), local(\"Times New Roman\");\n  size-adjust: 96.4%;\n  ascent-override: 98%;\n  descent-override: 24%;\n  line-gap-override: 0%;\n}\n\n:root {\n  --font-body: \"Source Serif Var\", \"Source Serif fallback\", Georgia, serif;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kio","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"kij","_type":"link","href":"https://screenspan.net/fallback"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kii","text":"The four numbers are per pair of fonts and you do not compute them by hand. Tools like ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kik","text":"Fallback Font Generator","marks":["kij"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kil","text":" or the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kim","text":"fontaine","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kin","text":" plugin measure both faces and print the declaration. Get them right and the swap becomes almost invisible: same line breaks, same page height, one change of shape.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kis","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kip","text":"If you would rather not fight at all, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kiq","text":"font-display: optional","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kir","text":" tells the browser to use the web font only if it is already cached or arrives within about 100 ms, and otherwise to keep the fallback for the whole visit. Zero shift, guaranteed, at the price of some first time visitors never seeing your typeface. For a text heavy site with returning readers, that trade is better than it sounds.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kiu","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kit","text":"Requests, and the one preload rule","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kiw","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kiv","text":"Preload exactly the fonts used above the fold, which for a text site means one, maybe two:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kix","language":"html","code":"<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"font\" type=\"font/woff2\"\n      href=\"/fonts/source-serif-latin.woff2\" crossorigin>"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kj1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kiy","text":"The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kiz","text":"crossorigin","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kj0","text":" attribute is mandatory even for a same origin file, because fonts are fetched in CORS mode; without it the browser downloads the file twice and you have made things worse while feeling clever. Preloading five fonts is the same mistake at scale: everything is high priority, so nothing is.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kj6","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"kj3","_type":"link","href":"https://fontsource.org"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kj2","text":"Self host. A third party font host means a DNS lookup, a TLS handshake and a second cache, and browsers have partitioned their HTTP cache since 2020, so the old shared cache argument for public CDNs is simply no longer true. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kj4","text":"Fontsource","marks":["kj3"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kj5","text":" packages the open families as npm modules with the subsets already cut.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kj8","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kj7","text":"So what does a second typeface cost?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kja","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kj9","text":"For that client, honestly: about 45 KB, one extra preload we could not afford, a fallback pair to calibrate, and the risk of a swap on the page that matters most to them. We shipped it anyway, and paid for it by dropping a weight they were not using. That is the whole discipline. Nothing is free, everything is worth it if you know the price, and the only unacceptable answer is not knowing.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'the-real-cost-of-a-web-font' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'what-a-good-brief-looks-like' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « What a good brief looks like » (en) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kjc","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjb","text":"We have run one hundred and six projects through this studio. I went back through the eleven that lost money and looked for the moment things turned. In nine of them, the moment was before the kickoff call. The brief did not contain the information the project needed, we started anyway because the client was pleasant and the work looked fun, and the missing information came back as scope in week seven.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kje","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjd","text":"A brief is not a wish list and it is not a specification. It is the smallest document that makes a decision possible, and it has to answer four questions.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kjg","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjf","text":"1. Who decides","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kji","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjh","text":"Not who is the client. Who, by name, can look at a page and say \"yes, ship it\", without asking anyone else.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kjk","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjj","text":"If the answer is a committee, the project does not have a decider, it has a queue, and every review round is the length of the slowest calendar in the group.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kjm","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjl","text":"If the answer is a name but that person has never been in a meeting with us, the answer is fictional and will be discovered in week five.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kjo","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjn","text":"If the answer is \"we will decide together\", that is a lovely sentiment and it means the first genuine disagreement has no resolution procedure.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kjq","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjp","text":"The fix is small and it works: one named decider, an agreed review cadence, and a written rule that feedback arrives consolidated from that person rather than as five separate emails that contradict each other. We put it in the brief in one sentence, and we read it out loud at kickoff so nobody can be surprised later.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kjs","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjr","text":"2. What already exists","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kju","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjt","text":"Half of every estimate is really an inventory question. A brief that says \"redesign the site\" is describing an unknown quantity of work; a brief with an inventory is describing a project.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t46","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r47","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c48","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjv","text":"Thing","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c49","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjx","text":"Who provides it","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4a","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kjz","text":"Needed by","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk1","text":"If it is late","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r4c","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk3","text":"Final copy, all pages","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk5","text":"Client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk7","text":"Week 3","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kk9","text":"Launch moves, day for day","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r4h","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4i","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkb","text":"Photography and logo files","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkd","text":"Client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkf","text":"Week 2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkh","text":"We use placeholders, one revision covered","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r4m","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4n","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkj","text":"Brand guidelines, if any","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkl","text":"Client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkn","text":"Week 1","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4q","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkp","text":"We propose, client approves in week 2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r4r","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4s","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkr","text":"Analytics and DNS access","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkt","text":"Client IT","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkv","text":"Week 8","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkx","text":"Launch moves","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r4w","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kkz","text":"Design, build, deployment","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kl1","text":"Studio","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c4z","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kl3","text":"Per plan","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c50","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kl5","text":"We eat it","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kl8","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kl7","text":"That last column is the one that changes behaviour. Not as a threat: it is written in the same sentence as our own penalty, which is that anything on our line is our problem and our cost. People accept a rule that visibly binds both sides, and a schedule that only slips in one direction is not a schedule, it is a hope.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kla","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kl9","text":"3. What counts as done","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klc","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klb","text":"\"Done\" is the most expensive undefined word in this industry. Ours is a list a client can check without us in the room:","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kle","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kld","text":"Every page in the agreed sitemap exists, with final content, in both languages.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klj","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[{"_key":"klg","_type":"link","href":"/blog/a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact/"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klf","text":"The site meets the ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"klh","text":"performance budget","marks":["klg"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kli","text":" on the agreed test device.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kll","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klk","text":"Keyboard navigation works end to end, and the automated accessibility pass is clean on all templates.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kln","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klm","text":"Analytics, redirects from the old URLs, and the sitemap are live and verified.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klp","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klo","text":"The client’s team has done the CMS walkthrough and edited one real page unsupervised.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klq","text":"Point five is worth more than the other four. A site that the client cannot edit is a site that dies in eighteen months, and the walkthrough is where you find out that the person who will actually maintain it was never in any of the meetings.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klt","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kls","text":"A deliverable that only the studio can verify is not a deliverable. It is a promise with extra steps.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klv","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klu","text":"4. What happens when we disagree","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"klw","text":"Every project has one. Usually it is the homepage, usually in week six, usually because two people wanted different things and both heard yes.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"klz","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kly","text":"We write the procedure in advance, in three lines: the decider decides; if the decision changes agreed scope, we quote the change before doing it; if the change is refused, the previously agreed version ships. That is it. It has never once felt heavy in practice, and the projects that had it were the ones where nobody had to raise their voice.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"km1","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"km0","text":"The three questions that reveal a budget","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"km3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"km2","text":"Clients often will not name a number, and the reason is reasonable: they think it becomes the price. So we ask three questions that produce the same information without anyone losing face.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"km6","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"km4","text":"\"What is the cost of doing nothing for another year?\"","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"km5","text":" The answer tells you the size of the problem in the client’s own units, which is the only unit that matters.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"km9","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"km7","text":"\"What else is this money competing with internally?\"","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"km8","text":" If it is competing with a hire, you are in the tens of thousands. If it is competing with a conference stand, you are in the low thousands, and you should say so kindly and quickly.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmc","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kma","text":"\"What did the last version cost, and what went wrong with it?\"","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kmb","text":" You learn the order of magnitude and the trauma at the same time, and the second half is usually more useful than the first.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kme","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmd","text":"Three answers, no number named, and you know within a factor of two whether the conversation is worth continuing. That is a kindness to both parties: the worst outcome in a first meeting is not a lost project, it is a project you take on at a number that guarantees resentment by week nine.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmg","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmf","text":"Content is the deadline","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmi","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmh","text":"If I could put one sentence on the first page of every brief it would be this one, because it is the single most reliable predictor of a project running late, and it is almost never the thing anyone worries about at the start: the design will be finished long before the words are, the build will be finished before the words are, the client will genuinely intend to write the words, and then the person who was going to write them will be pulled onto something urgent in another department, and the site will sit at ninety five percent complete for six weeks while everyone waits for a page of copy that nobody has been given time to write, and at the end of those six weeks somebody will suggest launching with placeholder text, and that is how sites end up shipping with a headline that says \"About us\" over three sentences from the 2019 brochure. Put content dates in the brief, give them owners, and treat a missed copy deadline exactly like a missed technical one.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmk","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmj","text":"The one page we send back","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmp","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"kmm","_type":"link","href":"https://www.gov.uk/service-manual"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kml","text":"After a first call we send a single page: the four answers as we understood them, the inventory table, the definition of done, and a price range with what moves it up or down. It takes forty minutes to write and it has never failed to be useful. Either the client corrects it, which is the cheapest correction the project will ever get, or they sign it, and we begin a project that already knows what it is. The ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kmn","text":"GOV.UK Service Manual","marks":["kmm"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kmo","text":" says something similar at considerably greater length, and it has been right for a decade.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'what-a-good-brief-looks-like' AND locale = 'en' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Un budget de performance qui résiste au client » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kmr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmq","text":"Tous les studios disent qu’ils tiennent à la performance. Presque aucun n’est capable de dire, avant le début du projet, quel nombre le pousserait à refuser une fonctionnalité. C’est là qu’est tout le problème : sans seuil convenu à l’avance, « rapide » est une affaire de goût, et le goût perd toutes ses discussions contre un service marketing.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmt","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kms","text":"Nous avons commencé à inscrire un budget de performance dans le devis en 2023. Il a échoué deux fois, et ces deux échecs nous ont appris plus que les réussites.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmv","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmu","text":"Les quatre nombres","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kmx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmw","text":"Un budget à neuf métriques est une liste de vœux. Le nôtre en compte quatre, et chacune existe parce qu’elle protège quelqu’un de différent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t51","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r52","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c53","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kmy","text":"Métrique","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c54","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kn0","text":"Cible","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c55","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kn2","text":"Protège","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r56","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c57","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kn4","text":"Largest Contentful Paint","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c58","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kn6","text":"2,0 s au p75[^p75]","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c59","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kn8","text":"La personne qui décide si elle reste","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5a","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kna","text":"Interaction to Next Paint","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"knc","text":"200 ms au p75","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kne","text":"Celle qui ouvre le menu sur un téléphone bas de gamme","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5e","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kng","text":"Cumulative Layout Shift","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kni","text":"0,05","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5h","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"knk","text":"Celle qui vient de perdre sa ligne","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5i","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"knm","text":"Poids de la page, gabarit d’article","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kno","text":"180 Ko compressés","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"knq","text":"Le client, contre nous","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"knt","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kns","text":"La dernière ligne est celle sur laquelle les clients posent des questions, et c’est celle qui nous importe le plus. Les trois Core Web Vitals sont des résultats : ils bougent pour des raisons que vous ne maîtrisez pas entièrement, y compris le CDN, le réseau du visiteur et le téléphone qu’il a en poche. Le poids de la page, lui, est une entrée. C’est le nombre que l’équipe fixe réellement, chaque jour, à chaque décision, et le seul qu’on puisse vérifier sans rien déployer.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"knv","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"knu","text":"[^p75]: Le p75, c’est le 75e centile des visites réelles : trois lecteurs sur quatre obtiennent cette expérience ou mieux. Les données de terrain de Chrome l’agrègent sur une fenêtre glissante de 28 jours, ce qui explique aussi pourquoi le correctif livré mardi dernier n’apparaît pas encore dans le rapport.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"knx","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"knw","text":"L’appareil fait partie du nombre","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"knz","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kny","text":"Une cible sans appareil n’est pas une cible. « LCP sous deux secondes » mesuré sur un MacBook branché à la fibre du bureau est une information sur notre bureau, pas sur le site.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ko1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ko0","text":"Nous mesurons sur un téléphone Android de milieu de gamme vieux de trois ans, sur une connexion bridée, et nous l’écrivons noir sur blanc. Concrètement, cela revient à un bridage processeur d’environ 4x et à un profil réseau proche d’une 4G lente, ce que simule par défaut le préréglage mobile de Lighthouse. La première fois qu’un client voit son propre site dans ces conditions, la réunion change complètement de nature. Plus personne n’a besoin d’être convaincu ensuite, et aucune présentation n’a jamais fait ce travail aussi bien.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ko3","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ko2","text":"L’écrire là où le build peut le lire","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ko5","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ko4","text":"Un budget que personne n’automatise expire discrètement vers la sixième semaine. Le nôtre vit dans un fichier :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"ko6","language":"json","code":"[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"/*\",\n    \"resourceSizes\": [\n      { \"resourceType\": \"document\", \"budget\": 20 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"script\", \"budget\": 40 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"stylesheet\", \"budget\": 25 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"font\", \"budget\": 95 },\n      { \"resourceType\": \"total\", \"budget\": 400 }\n    ],\n    \"resourceCounts\": [\n      { \"resourceType\": \"third-party\", \"budget\": 4 }\n    ],\n    \"timings\": [\n      { \"metric\": \"largest-contentful-paint\", \"budget\": 2000 },\n      { \"metric\": \"cumulative-layout-shift\", \"budget\": 0.05 }\n    ]\n  }\n]"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ko8","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ko7","text":"Les tailles sont en kibioctets, les temps en millisecondes, et le fichier est compris directement par la ligne de commande Lighthouse :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"ko9","language":"bash","code":"npx lighthouse \"https://recette.example.com/journal/premier-article/\" \\\n  --budget-path=./perf/budget.json \\\n  --form-factor=mobile \\\n  --output=json --output-path=./perf/rapport.json \\\n  --chrome-flags=\"--headless=new\""},{"_type":"block","_key":"kob","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"koa","text":"Le contrôle tourne sur chaque pull request qui touche aux gabarits, et le job échoue sur un dépassement de budget, pas sur un score. Un score est une moyenne pondérée qui change d’une version de Lighthouse à l’autre ; un budget est une promesse avec une unité. Quand le nombre bouge, la pull request vous dit quel type de ressource l’a fait bouger, et la discussion prend deux minutes au lieu d’un après-midi.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kod","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"koc","text":"La clause qui fait le vrai travail","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kof","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"koe","text":"L’automatisation attrape les régressions. Elle ne répond pas à la question politique, qui arrive toujours vers la semaine neuf et paraît toujours raisonnable. C’est le contrat qui y répond :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"koi","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kog","text":"Le budget est une quantité fixe, pas un objectif.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"koh","text":" On ne demande à personne d’être en dessous en moyenne.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kol","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"koj","text":"Tout poids ajouté oblige à retirer l’équivalent.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kok","text":" Une vidéo d’en-tête de 90 Ko passe si 90 Ko d’autre chose partent, et c’est le client qui choisit quoi.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"koo","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kom","text":"Les tiers comptent comme les nôtres.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kon","text":" Une balise de mesure d’audience, un module de discussion et un gestionnaire de consentement font trois des quatre tiers autorisés : le quatrième est donc une décision, pas un accident.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kor","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kop","text":"Un dépassement bloque la mise en ligne, il ne devient pas un ticket.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"koq","text":" Le site part lent ou il part plus tard. Il n’y a pas de troisième option, ni de backlog où le faire disparaître.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kot","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kos","text":"L’intérêt de coucher cela sur le papier n’est pas juridique. Nous ne l’avons jamais brandi. Sa vraie fonction, c’est de déplacer la discussion de la semaine neuf, quand le budget est consommé et tout le monde fatigué, à la semaine zéro, quand elle reste abstraite entre gens qui s’apprécient encore.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kov","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kou","text":"Là où nos budgets ont échoué","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kox","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kow","text":"Deux fois, et pour la même raison : le site avait quitté nos mains.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"koz","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"koy","text":"Les balises que personne ne surveillait","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kp1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kp0","text":"Premier échec, un client dont l’équipe marketing a ajouté six balises via un gestionnaire de balises le mois suivant la mise en ligne. Le poids de la page a triplé. Rien dans notre processus ne surveillait quoi que ce soit, puisque notre automatisation tournait sur les pull requests, et qu’il n’y avait plus de pull requests. Aujourd’hui, le même passage de Lighthouse tourne chaque semaine contre la production, et le rapport arrive dans la boîte du client, pas dans la nôtre.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kp3","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kp2","text":"La photo de quatre mégaoctets","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kp5","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kp4","text":"Deuxième échec, un problème de contenu déguisé en problème technique. Une rédactrice a téléversé une photo de 4,2 Mo via le CMS, qui l’a poliment redimensionnée pour l’affichage et a tout de même servi l’original sur la page d’article, parce que le gabarit demandait le fichier source. C’est notre bug, pas le sien, et le correctif a été une chaîne de traitement qui rend l’erreur impossible : tout téléversement est transcodé en AVIF et en WebP avec des dimensions explicites, et le gabarit ne peut plus référencer un fichier original du tout.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kp7","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kp6","text":"Les deux échecs ont une forme commune qui mérite un nom. Un budget protège le code que vous écrivez. Il ne fait rien contre les contenus et les balises qui arrivent après, et c’est pourtant là que le poids s’accumule sur la vie d’un site. Si vous ne mettez en place qu’un seul contrôle automatique après la mise en ligne, n’en faites pas un test synthétique de votre propre gabarit. Faites-en un passage hebdomadaire sur la page en ligne, sur le téléphone que vos lecteurs utilisent vraiment, envoyé à la personne qui a le pouvoir de dire non.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kp9","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kp8","text":"Ce que ça coûte","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kpb","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpa","text":"Un après-midi en début de projet, un job d’intégration continue d’une trentaine de lignes, et la discipline de laisser un build échouer un vendredi. En échange, vous obtenez un site encore rapide à la fin de la mission, la seule mesure que fasse jamais quelqu’un d’extérieur à l’équipe.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'a-type-scale-you-can-defend' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Une échelle typographique défendable » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kpd","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpc","text":"Demandez à un designer d’où vient son échelle typographique et vous obtenez en général une proportion : une tierce majeure, une quarte juste, le nombre d’or si le projet a de l’ambition. Demandez à quoi sert le quatrième palier et la pièce devient silencieuse.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kpf","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpe","text":"Une proportion est une façon de produire des candidats. Ce n’est pas une décision de design, et ça ne peut pas l’être, puisqu’elle ignore ce qu’il y a sur votre page. Les échelles qui survivent au contact du contenu réel sont celles où chaque palier a un rôle, et où la personne qui les a choisis sait dire ce qui casse si l’on en supprime un.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kph","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpg","text":"Cinq paliers, cinq rôles","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kpj","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpi","text":"Voici l’échelle de ce carnet. Cinq tailles, dont une utilisée exactement une fois par page.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t5m","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5n","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpk","text":"Palier","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpm","text":"Rôle","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5q","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpo","text":"Mobile","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5r","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpq","text":"Bureau","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5s","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kps","text":"Interligne","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5t","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpu","text":"Titre","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpw","text":"Le titre de l’article, une fois","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5w","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kpy","text":"32 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kq0","text":"56 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c5y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kq2","text":"1,05","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r5z","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c60","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kq4","text":"Section","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c61","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kq6","text":"h2, la carte du lecteur","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c62","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kq8","text":"24 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c63","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqa","text":"30 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c64","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqc","text":"1,2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r65","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c66","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqe","text":"Sous-titre","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c67","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqg","text":"h3 et h4, rares","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c68","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqi","text":"20 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c69","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqk","text":"22 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6a","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqm","text":"1,3","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r6b","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqo","text":"Labeur","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqq","text":"Tout ce qu’on lit vraiment","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqs","text":"18 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqu","text":"19 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqw","text":"1,6","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r6h","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6i","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kqy","text":"Annexe","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kr0","text":"Dates, légendes, notes","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kr2","text":"15 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kr4","text":"15 px","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6m","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kr6","text":"1,5","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kr9","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kr8","text":"Deux choix de ce tableau méritent discussion, alors défendons-les.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krb","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kra","text":"Le texte de labeur démarre à 18 px, pas à 16. Le défaut de 16 px est une convention de navigateur héritée des écrans de bureau à 96 ppp, et sur un téléphone tenu à bout de bras, c’est petit. Chaque fois que nous avons augmenté la taille du texte courant sur un site client, le temps de lecture a monté, et personne n’a jamais écrit pour se plaindre que le texte était trop grand.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krd","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krc","text":"Le texte d’annexe ne rétrécit pas davantage sur mobile. C’est dans les petites tailles que l’accessibilité échoue discrètement, et 15 px est notre plancher. Si quelque chose doit passer sous le plancher pour tenir, c’est la mise en page qui est fausse, pas la typographie.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krf","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kre","text":"La proportion est un point de départ qu’on a le droit de casser","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krh","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krg","text":"Une proportion de 1,25 à partir d’une base de 18 px donne 18 ; 22,5 ; 28 ; 35 ; 44. C’est propre, et inutile en haut : 44 px n’est pas un titre, c’est un gros intertitre, et la page n’a plus de moment d’arrivée. Nous cassons donc la proportion au palier de titre et sautons à 56, parce que ce palier a un rôle différent du reste de l’échelle. Ce n’est pas « une taille au-dessus d’un intertitre », c’est ce qui annonce que l’article commence.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krj","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kri","text":"En bas de l’échelle, nous arrondissons au pixel entier plutôt que de traîner les décimales de la proportion. Les tailles sous-pixel existent vraiment et les navigateurs les rendent, mais elles servent surtout à faire croire que 22,4 px et 22 px sont deux décisions de design différentes. Elles ne le sont pas.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krl","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krk","text":"Paliers calculés par la proportion : labeur, sous-titre, section.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krn","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krm","text":"Paliers posés à la main : titre (c’est une affiche) et annexe (c’est un plancher).","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krp","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kro","text":"Paliers supprimés : deux, parce qu’aucun gabarit ne les utilisait, et une échelle inutilisée produit de l’incohérence dès que quelqu’un a besoin d’une taille qui n’y est pas.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krr","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krq","text":"Fluide, sans magie","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"krv","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krs","text":"Entre les deux colonnes du tableau se trouve ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"krt","text":"clamp()","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kru","text":", et il vaut la peine de l’écrire pour qu’un humain puisse le lire.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"krw","language":"css","code":":root {\n  /* 32px a 320px de large, 56px a 1240px, lineaire entre les deux. */\n  --step-display: clamp(2rem, 1.478rem + 2.609vw, 3.5rem);\n  --step-section: clamp(1.5rem, 1.37rem + 0.652vw, 1.875rem);\n  --step-body:    clamp(1.125rem, 1.103rem + 0.109vw, 1.1875rem);\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kry","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"krx","text":"La valeur du milieu n’est pas un nombre magique, c’est une droite qui passe par deux points. La pente est l’écart de taille divisé par l’écart de largeur, et l’ordonnée à l’origine est ce qui reste quand on retranche la contribution de la pente au bord inférieur :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"krz","code":"pente     = (56 - 32) / (1240 - 320) = 0,02609  ->  2.609vw\nordonnee  = 32 - (0,02609 x 320)     = 23,65px  ->  1.478rem"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ks1","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ks0","text":"Deux règles qui gardent tout cela honnête","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksh","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"ksb","_type":"link","href":"https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/resize-text.html"},{"_key":"kse","_type":"link","href":"https://utopia.fyi"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ks2","text":"Écrivez l’ordonnée en ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks3","text":"rem","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks4","text":", jamais en ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks5","text":"px","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks6","text":", pour que l’expression entière réagisse encore quand un lecteur augmente la taille de police par défaut de son navigateur ; un clamp bâti uniquement sur des ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks7","text":"px","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks8","text":" et des ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ks9","text":"vw","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksa","text":" ignore cette préférence et échoue discrètement au critère ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksc","text":"WCAG 1.4.4","marks":["ksb"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksd","text":". Et ne laissez jamais la plage fluide couvrir tout le design : sous 320 et au-dessus de 1240, la valeur se verrouille, ce qui est exactement souhaitable sur un écran de 1900 px où un titre qui continue de grossir devient un panneau publicitaire. Si l’arithmétique vous ennuie, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksf","text":"Utopia","marks":["kse"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksg","text":" génère les mêmes expressions à partir des mêmes quatre entrées.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksj","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ksi","text":"Les trois mots dont on discute réellement","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksl","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ksk","text":"<dl> <dt>Longueur de ligne</dt> <dd>La largeur d’une ligne de texte, comptée en caractères. De 60 à 75 est la plage confortable pour de la prose suivie ; sous 45 l’œil saute trop souvent, au-dessus de 85 il perd le début de la ligne suivante. Réglez-la en ch et elle suivra la police.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksn","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ksm","text":"  <dt>Interligne</dt> <dd>L’espace entre les lignes, exprimé en line-height sans unité pour qu’il se multiplie par la taille propre de l’élément. Il doit croître quand la ligne s’allonge et diminuer quand la typographie grossit : 1,6 pour le texte courant, 1,05 pour un grand titre.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksp","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kso","text":"  <dt>Approche</dt> <dd>L’espacement uniforme entre les lettres. Les grandes tailles réclament presque toujours une approche légèrement négative, les petites tailles et les capitales une approche positive. C’est le réglage vers lequel on se précipite en premier et dont on a le moins besoin.</dd> </dl>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ksq","text":"En CSS, cela fait quatre déclarations, et elles font plus pour la lisibilité que n’importe quel choix de caractère :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kss","language":"css","code":".prose {\n  max-inline-size: 68ch;\n  font-size: var(--step-body);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n  text-wrap: pretty;\n}\n\n.prose h1 {\n  font-size: var(--step-display);\n  line-height: 1.05;\n  letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n  text-wrap: balance;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kst","text":"text-wrap: balance","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksu","text":" égalise les lignes d’un titre court pour éviter les cinq mots suivis d’un seul. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksv","text":"text-wrap: pretty","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ksw","text":" fait le travail plus modeste sur le texte courant, en empêchant le mot orphelin en fin de paragraphe. Ce sont des indications plutôt que des garanties, et les deux ne coûtent rien là où elles ne sont pas gérées.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ksz","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ksy","text":"Le tester sur les deux largeurs qui comptent","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kt1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kt0","text":"Une échelle qui n’a l’air juste que dans le fichier de maquette n’est pas une échelle. La nôtre est vérifiée sur exactement deux largeurs, avec du contenu réel : 320 px, parce que c’est encore le téléphone le plus étroit dans les données de terrain, et 1440 px, parce que c’est là qu’un titre long a de la place pour vous ridiculiser.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kt3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kt2","text":"Les tests sont volontairement ennuyeux :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kt5","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kt4","text":"Le plus long titre d’article réel tient-il en trois lignes à 320 px sans couper un mot ?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kt7","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kt6","text":"À 1440 px, la ligne fait-elle toujours moins de 75 caractères, ou le conteneur a-t-il grandi en douce ?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kt9","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kt8","text":"La page tient-elle encore debout à 200 % de zoom navigateur, question qui revient à demander si une taille est verrouillée en px ?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ktb","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kta","text":"Deux paliers voisins se distinguent-ils assez pour qu’un lecteur reconnaisse une section d’une sous-section sans compter les pixels ?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ktd","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktc","text":"La question qui tue les échelles","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kti","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"ktf","_type":"link","href":"/fr/blog/the-real-cost-of-a-web-font/"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kte","text":"C’est la quatrième qui s’en charge. Si vous ne voyez pas la différence, vous n’avez pas deux paliers, vous avez un palier et une erreur d’arrondi, et le remède est d’en supprimer un plutôt que d’ajouter du contraste ailleurs. Le ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ktg","text":"coût d’une seconde police","marks":["ktf"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kth","text":" est une autre discussion, mais une échelle qui en réclame une pour être lisible n’a jamais été une échelle.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'a-type-scale-you-can-defend' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'dark-mode-is-a-content-problem' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Le mode sombre est un problème de contenu » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"ktm","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktj","text":"Tous les devis de mode sombre que j’ai écrits se sont trompés dans le même sens. Les couleurs prennent un après-midi. Le mois part dans ce qui n’est pas de la couleur : un logo client avec un fond blanc incrusté, une bibliothèque de graphiques qui code en dur ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ktk","text":"#333","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ktl","text":", une photo de produit sur fond blanc infini qui perce désormais un trou dans la page, et un corail de marque qui paraissait sûr de lui sur le papier et devient radioactif à neuf heures du soir.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kto","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktn","text":"Le mode sombre n’est pas un thème. C’est une seconde édition du contenu.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ktq","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktp","text":"La palette est vraiment la partie facile","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kts","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktr","text":"Deux fonctionnalités CSS ont supprimé l’essentiel de la plomberie.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ktu","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktt","text":"D’abord, dites au navigateur ce que vous savez faire, pour que les contrôles de formulaire, les barres de défilement, les soulignements du correcteur et le fond par défaut cessent de vous contredire :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"ktv","language":"css","code":":root {\n  color-scheme: light dark;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ktx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktw","text":"Ensuite, laissez une seule déclaration porter les deux valeurs :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kty","language":"css","code":":root {\n  --surface: light-dark(oklch(99% 0.005 250), oklch(21% 0.02 250));\n  --text: light-dark(oklch(28% 0.02 250), oklch(92% 0.01 250));\n  --border: light-dark(oklch(90% 0.01 250), oklch(32% 0.02 250));\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"ku3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ktz","text":"light-dark()","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ku0","text":" choisit une valeur selon le schéma de couleurs utilisé, et ne fonctionne que si ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ku1","text":"color-scheme","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ku2","text":" est renseigné, ce qui est une jolie idée de conception d’API : la fonction refuse de marcher tant que vous n’avez pas écrit la déclaration qui répare de toute façon les widgets natifs.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ku5","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ku4","text":"Si l’on écrit ces valeurs en OKLCH plutôt qu’en hexadécimal, c’est parce que le premier nombre y est la clarté perçue. Inverser une palette hexadécimale en retournant les chiffres produit des couleurs mathématiquement opposées et visuellement fausses, parce que le sRGB n’a aucune idée de la luminosité qu’un humain croit voir. En OKLCH, on peut dire « même teinte, même chroma, clarté 21 au lieu de 99 » et obtenir un résultat qui se lit comme la même couleur dans une autre pièce.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ku7","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ku6","text":"Une correction qui surprend : en mode sombre, du blanc pur sur du noir pur est pire, pas mieux. Ça vibre, ça bave pour les lecteurs astigmates, et ça fatigue sur un article long. Nos valeurs par défaut tournent autour de 92 % de clarté sur 21 %, ce qui donne un fort contraste sans l’éblouissement.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ku9","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ku8","text":"Ce que la palette ne contrôle pas","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kub","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kua","text":"Voici la liste qui consomme réellement le budget.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kug","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kuc","text":"Les photos sur fond blanc.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kud","text":" Un packshot sur fond blanc infini devient un rectangle de plein jour au milieu d’une page sombre. Soit vous obtenez des détourages avec transparence, soit vous acceptez un petit compromis : ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kue","text":"filter: brightness(0.92) contrast(1.02)","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kuf","text":" casse l’agressivité sans changer visiblement le produit.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kuj","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kuh","text":"Les captures d’écran.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kui","text":" La capture d’une interface claire ne se rattrape pas au filtre, et l’inverser est un mensonge. Soit on photographie l’interface deux fois, soit on la pose sur une carte volontairement claire dans les deux modes, cadrée pour qu’elle se lise comme une citation.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kuo","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kuk","text":"Les graphiques et les schémas.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kul","text":" Tout ce qui a des couleurs de trait codées en dur réclame une vraie variante sombre. Le SVG est le seul format raisonnable ici, parce qu’il peut hériter de ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kum","text":"currentColor","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kun","text":" et cesser complètement d’être un problème d’image.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kur","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kup","text":"Les blocs de code.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kuq","text":" Deux thèmes, commutés avec le reste de la page. Un bloc clair sur un article sombre est la première chose qu’un développeur remarque et la dernière qu’il pardonne.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kuu","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kus","text":"Les intégrations tierces.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kut","text":" Lecteurs vidéo, cartes, modules de commentaires et bandeaux de consentement ont chacun leur avis. Certains acceptent un paramètre. D’autres non. Prévoyez du budget pour ceux qui refusent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kux","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kuv","text":"La couleur de marque.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kuw","text":" Celle-là mérite sa propre section.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kuz","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kuy","text":"La couleur de marque aura besoin d’une jumelle","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kv1","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kv0","text":"Une valeur d’accentuation unique ne peut pas servir les deux modes. Voici le corail de nos propres tokens, mesuré sur les deux fonds :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t6n","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r6o","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kv2","text":"Couleur","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6q","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kv4","text":"Sur fond clair","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6r","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kv6","text":"Sur fond sombre","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r6s","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kv8","text":"Corail 55","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kva","text":"4,7:1, passe pour du texte courant","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvc","text":"2,1:1, échoue partout","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r6w","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kve","text":"Corail 72","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvg","text":"2,3:1, échoue","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c6z","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvi","text":"6,4:1, passe confortablement","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kvn","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvk","text":"Aucune valeur unique de cette colonne ne fonctionne deux fois. La solution honnête, ce sont deux tokens sous un seul nom sémantique : ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kvl","text":"--accent","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kvm","text":" vaut Corail 55 en clair et Corail 72 en sombre, et le balisage ne sait jamais lequel il a reçu. Les WCAG demandent 4,5:1 pour le texte courant et 3:1 pour les grands textes et les parties visibles des composants d’interface : une couleur de lien qui ne passe que dans un mode est une couleur qui échoue pour la moitié de votre lectorat.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kvr","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvo","text":"Si un token réclame une surcharge ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kvp","text":"dark:","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kvq","text":" dans le balisage, c’est le token qui est faux. Corrigez la couche qui définit la couleur, pas les onze endroits qui l’utilisent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kvt","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvs","text":"Le clignotement, et le seul script que nous autorisons","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kvv","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvu","text":"Un thème qui respecte une préférence enregistrée pose un vrai problème : le serveur ne connaît pas cette préférence, donc le premier rendu peut être faux. Le remède est un petit script bloquant dans le head, et c’est l’un des rares endroits où un script bloquant est la bonne réponse :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kvw","language":"astro","code":"---\n// src/components/ThemeInit.astro - s''exécute avant le premier rendu, volontairement.\n---\n\n<script is:inline>\n  const stored = localStorage.getItem(\"theme\");\n  const dark = stored\n    ? stored === \"dark\"\n    : window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\").matches;\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle(\"dark\", dark);\n</script>"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kvy","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvx","text":"Deux pièges en sept lignes","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kw6","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kvz","text":"Deux détails nous ont coûté un bug chacun. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kw0","text":"is:inline","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kw1","text":" est obligatoire, sans quoi le bundler déplace le script et il ne s’exécute plus avant le rendu. Et si le site utilise les view transitions, l’échange remplace les attributs de l’élément ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kw2","text":"<html>","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kw3","text":" par ceux rendus côté serveur : il faut donc réappliquer la classe sur ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kw4","text":"astro:after-swap","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kw5","text":", sinon la page repasse en clair au deuxième clic.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kw8","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kw7","text":"Tant que vous êtes dans le head, livrez l’habillage de navigateur qui va avec :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kw9","language":"html","code":"<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#fbfaf8\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#131a22\" media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\">"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kwb","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwa","text":"C’est la barre d’adresse sur Safari et Chrome mobiles. Le rater, c’est la différence entre un site qui a l’air dessiné et un site qui a l’air d’un document imprimé dans un navigateur.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kwd","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwc","text":"Ce que nous disons aux clients désormais","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kwf","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwe","text":"Le mode sombre est chiffré comme un livrable de contenu, pas comme une tâche de mise en forme, et le devis comprend trois lignes actionnables : un jeu d’images à fond transparent, une décision sur la couleur de marque en contexte sombre, et une personne nommée qui regardera les dix pages les plus visitées dans les deux modes avant la mise en ligne.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kwh","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwg","text":"Le dernier point n’est pas une plaisanterie. Tous les bugs de mode sombre que nous avons livrés se trouvaient sur une page que personne n’avait pensé à regarder deux fois : une page de mentions légales avec un style de tableau hérité, une 404 avec une image de fond, un gabarit d’e-mail qui ne fait même pas partie du site. La palette est un système, et les systèmes sont bons sur les pages que vous avez dessinées. Le contenu n’est pas un système, et il vous attendra sur la page que vous avez oubliée.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'dark-mode-is-a-content-problem' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'measuring-what-the-reader-feels' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Le chargement mesuré chez le lecteur, pas au labo » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kwj","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwi","text":"L’automne dernier, le site d’un client affichait 98 sur Lighthouse et un Largest Contentful Paint de 1,4 seconde sur nos passages de test. Le même site, dans les données de terrain de Chrome, se tenait à 3,9 secondes au 75e centile. Les deux chiffres étaient exacts. C’étaient les réponses à deux questions différentes, et une seule des deux questions portait sur les lecteurs du client.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kwl","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwk","text":"C’est cet écart qui nous fait installer aujourd’hui une mesure de terrain sur chaque site que nous livrons, avant la mise en ligne, comme partie du projet et non comme rattrapage.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kwn","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwm","text":"Deux instruments, deux métiers","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t70","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r71","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c73","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"s72","text":"","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c74","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwo","text":"Laboratoire (synthétique)","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c75","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwq","text":"Terrain (vrais visiteurs)","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r76","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c77","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kws","text":"Qui est mesuré","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c78","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwu","text":"Une visite scriptée","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c79","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kww","text":"Tout le monde, sur son propre appareil","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r7a","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kwy","text":"Réseau","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kx0","text":"Simulé, constant","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kx2","text":"Celui qu’ils ont","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r7e","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kx4","text":"Excellent pour","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kx6","text":"Attraper les régressions, comparer deux builds","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7h","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kx8","text":"Dire ce qui se passe réellement","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r7i","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxa","text":"Aveugle à","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxc","text":"Caches, bandeaux de consentement, sessions connectées, géographie","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxe","text":"Tout ce que personne n’a encore visité","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r7m","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7n","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxg","text":"Disponible","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxi","text":"Avant la mise en ligne","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxk","text":"Après, avec du retard","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kxn","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxm","text":"L’erreur n’est pas d’utiliser l’un des deux. L’erreur est de croire qu’un bon chiffre du premier dit quelque chose du second. Le laboratoire est une expérience contrôlée : on change une chose, on regarde ce qui bouge. Le terrain est une observation du réel, et le réel comprend le lecteur qui a ouvert votre article dans un train, sur un téléphone de quatre ans, derrière un bandeau de consentement, avec un mode économie d’énergie qui bride le processeur.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kxp","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxo","text":"Les trois métriques qui valent la peine","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kxr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxq","text":"Les Core Web Vitals sont au nombre de trois parce que c’est à peu près le nombre de choses indépendantes qu’un lecteur peut remarquer.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kxu","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxs","text":"LCP","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kxt","text":" répond à « est-ce que l’essentiel est apparu ». Le seuil publié est 2,5 secondes au p75 ; nous visons 2,0 pour garder de la marge.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kxx","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxv","text":"INP","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kxw","text":" répond à « est-ce que la page a réagi quand j’ai touché l’écran ». Il a remplacé le First Input Delay en mars 2024 et il est bien plus difficile à truquer, puisqu’il regarde toutes les interactions de la visite et non la première seulement. Sous 200 ms.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ky0","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kxy","text":"CLS","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kxz","text":" répond à « est-ce que la page a bougé pendant ma lecture ». Sous 0,1, et l’objectif honnête est zéro.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ky2","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ky1","text":"Nous ne collectons rien d’autre au premier passage. Les métriques supplémentaires sont surtout une façon d’éviter la conclusion que les trois premières ont déjà donnée.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ky4","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ky3","text":"Le dispositif honnête le plus simple","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"ky9","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"ky6","_type":"link","href":"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"ky5","text":"Aucun prestataire de mesure, aucun gestionnaire de balises, un point d’entrée à nous. Tout le code client tient en une vingtaine de lignes, avec la variante « attribution » de ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ky7","text":"web-vitals","marks":["ky6"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"ky8","text":", qui vous dit non seulement que quelque chose a été lent, mais quel élément en est responsable :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kya","language":"js","code":"import { onCLS, onINP, onLCP } from \"web-vitals/attribution\";\n\nconst queue = [];\n\nfunction record(metric) {\n  const a = metric.attribution;\n  queue.push({\n    name: metric.name,\n    // Le CLS est sans unité : on le stocke mis a l''echelle pour n''envoyer que des entiers.\n    value: Math.round(metric.name === \"CLS\" ? metric.value * 1000 : metric.value),\n    rating: metric.rating,\n    path: location.pathname,\n    culprit: a.interactionTarget ?? a.largestShiftTarget ?? a.element ?? null,\n    connection: navigator.connection?.effectiveType ?? null,\n  });\n}\n\nonLCP(record);\nonINP(record);\nonCLS(record);\n\naddEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", () => {\n  if (document.visibilityState !== \"hidden\" || queue.length === 0) return;\n  navigator.sendBeacon(\"/api/vitals\", JSON.stringify(queue.splice(0)));\n});"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kyc","style":"h3","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kyb","text":"Quatre choix délibérés","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kye","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kyd","text":"Quatre décisions y sont délibérées.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kyr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kyf","text":"sendBeacon","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyg","text":" plutôt que ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyh","text":"fetch","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyi","text":", parce qu’il survit à la fermeture de la page et ne retarde pas la navigation. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyj","text":"visibilitychange","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyk","text":" plutôt que ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyl","text":"unload","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kym","text":", parce que ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyn","text":"unload","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyo","text":" n’est pas fiable sur mobile et désactive le cache de retour arrière, ce qui ralentirait précisément les lecteurs que nous cherchons à aider.[^ordre] Le champ ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyp","text":"culprit","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyq","text":", parce que « INP à 480 ms » ouvre une enquête là où « INP à 480 ms sur le bouton de filtre par sujet » la referme. Et un taux d’échantillonnage, absent de l’extrait : sur un site à trafic réel, nous n’envoyons qu’une fraction tirée au hasard des sessions, parce que cent pour cent des visites font beaucoup de lignes pour n’apprendre rien de plus.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kyv","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kys","text":"[^ordre]: L’ordre compte ici. La bibliothèque web-vitals enregistre son propre écouteur ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyt","text":"visibilitychange","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kyu","text":" au moment de l’import et y finalise les valeurs en attente. Comme les écouteurs s’exécutent dans leur ordre d’enregistrement, importer la bibliothèque avant d’ajouter l’écouteur d’envoi est ce qui garantit que la file est pleine quand le beacon part.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kyx","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kyw","text":"Côté serveur, un gestionnaire valide la forme, jette tout ce qui porte un nom de métrique inconnu, et ajoute une ligne. Le nôtre écrit dans un fichier SQLite et une petite requête agrège le p75 par gabarit et par semaine. Il n’y a aucun produit de tableau de bord dans cette pile, et en deux ans il n’y a pas eu un moment où il nous en ait manqué un.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kyz","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kyy","text":"---","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kz1","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kz0","text":"Quand le laboratoire et le terrain se contredisent, c’est le terrain qui a raison","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kz3","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kz2","text":"Revenons au client à 1,4 seconde en laboratoire et 3,9 sur le terrain. Les données d’attribution ont rendu l’enquête courte.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kz5","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kz4","text":"L’élément LCP sur le terrain était l’image d’en-tête, et sa décomposition plaçait presque tout le temps dans le délai avant chargement de la ressource, pas dans le téléchargement lui-même. Autrement dit, le navigateur savait quoi récupérer et n’arrivait pas à commencer. En cause : un script de gestion du consentement chargé de façon synchrone dans le head, qui mettait 600 ms à arriver, puis écrivait des styles en ligne masquant l’en-tête jusqu’à la décision du visiteur. Nos passages de laboratoire ne l’ont jamais vu : notre profil de test avait déjà consenti, et le script se court-circuitait.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kz9","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kz6","text":"Le second contributeur était moins spectaculaire et plus fréquent : onze pour cent des visites arrivaient avec un type de connexion effectif ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kz7","text":"3g","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kz8","text":", depuis une région qui ne figurait sur la liste des marchés importants de personne et se révélait être leur deuxième source de commandes. Le p75 de toute l’audience était fixé par une audience que personne n’avait regardée.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzb","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kza","text":"Nous avons repoussé le script de consentement à un chargement différé avec une place réservée pour son bandeau, préchargé l’image d’en-tête, et servi de l’AVIF en trois largeurs. Le LCP de terrain au p75 est passé de 3,9 à 2,1 secondes sur les quatre semaines suivantes, délai inhérent à une fenêtre glissante de 28 jours plutôt qu’à un correctif lent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzd","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzc","text":"Deux vérifications qui ne coûtent rien","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzf","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kze","text":"Avant d’écrire la moindre ligne, passez cinq minutes sur les données de terrain publiques de l’origine. Si le site a assez de trafic, Chrome les a déjà collectées :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"kzg","language":"bash","code":"curl -s \"https://chromeuxreport.googleapis.com/v1/records:queryRecord?key=$CRUX_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ''{\"origin\":\"https://example.com\",\"formFactor\":\"PHONE\"}'' \\\n  | jq ''.record.metrics | to_entries[] | {(.key): .value.percentiles.p75}''"},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzl","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"kzi","_type":"link","href":"/fr/blog/a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact/"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzh","text":"Et gardez le test de laboratoire dans l’intégration continue, braqué sur le ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kzj","text":"budget de performance","marks":["kzi"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"kzk","text":" plutôt que sur un score. Les deux instruments font des métiers différents : le laboratoire vous dit que cette pull request a dégradé quelque chose, dans une comparaison que vous maîtrisez. Le terrain vous dit si le site est bon, dans la seule comparaison qui rapporte.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzn","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzm","text":"Si vous ne pouvez en garder qu’un, prenez le terrain. Il est moins pratique, il arrive en retard, il ne se lance pas sur une branche, et c’est le seul qui ait jamais fait changer d’avis un client.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'measuring-what-the-reader-feels' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'pricing-a-redesign-without-guessing' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Chiffrer une refonte sans deviner » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"kzp","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzo","text":"Il y a dans la facturation à l’heure un piège que j’ai mis quatre ans à voir. Plus vous devenez bon, moins vous gagnez pour le même travail. Vous maîtrisez la pile technique, vous fabriquez vos outils, vous cessez de commettre l’erreur de 2019, et la récompense est une facture qui baisse. Pendant ce temps, le client, qui se moque du temps qu’a pris le site, payait votre inexpérience précisément au moment où vous avez cessé d’en avoir.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzr","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzq","text":"L’heure est une unité de coût. Le client, lui, achète un résultat. Tout modèle de prix qui mesure la première et la vend comme le second finira par paraître injuste à quelqu’un, en général aux deux parties du même projet.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzt","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzs","text":"Trois prix, un seul projet","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"kzv","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzu","text":"Nous avons arrêté d’envoyer un seul chiffre en 2022. Chaque proposition en contient désormais trois, et ce ne sont pas trois tailles d’une même chose : ce sont trois projets différents qui règlent le même problème avec des degrés d’ambition différents.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t7q","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r7r","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"s7s","text":"","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzw","text":"Rhabillage","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"kzy","text":"Refonte","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7w","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k100","text":"Plateforme","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r7x","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k102","text":"De quoi il s’agit","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c7z","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k104","text":"Structure existante, nouvelle interface","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c80","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k106","text":"Nouvelle structure, nouveau modèle de contenu, nouvelle interface","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c81","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k108","text":"Refonte, plus outillage éditorial et design system","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r82","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c83","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10a","text":"Gabarits dessinés","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c84","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10c","text":"Jusqu’à 6","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c85","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10e","text":"Jusqu’à 12","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c86","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10g","text":"Gabarits et bibliothèque de composants","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r87","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c88","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10i","text":"Contenu","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c89","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10k","text":"Migré tel quel","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8a","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10m","text":"Restructuré avec le client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10o","text":"Restructuré, plus un flux de travail pour l’équipe","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r8c","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8d","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10q","text":"Durée type","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10s","text":"4 à 6 semaines","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10u","text":"8 à 12 semaines","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10w","text":"14 semaines et plus","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r8h","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8i","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k10y","text":"Fourchette","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k110","text":"6 à 9 k","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k112","text":"12 à 18 k","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k114","text":"25 k et plus","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k117","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k116","text":"Trois effets en découlent, et je n’en avais correctement prévu aucun.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k119","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k118","text":"Le premier : la conversation passe de « oui ou non » à « lequel », et c’est une bien meilleure conversation. Le deuxième : les clients choisissent l’option du milieu la plupart du temps, ce qui est largement documenté et un peu gênant à exploiter, donc nous veillons à ce que l’option du milieu soit sincèrement celle que nous recommanderions. Le troisième est le plus utile : le client qui choisit l’option la moins chère le fait en sachant ce qu’il n’aura pas, et il cesse de le réclamer en semaine sept, puisque c’est écrit comme appartenant à un autre prix.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11b","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11a","text":"Un devis unique n’appelle qu’une seule objection : le chiffre. Trois devis appellent une décision, et une décision est une conversation dans laquelle vous pouvez réellement aider.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11d","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11c","text":"Ce que nous écrivons au sujet des allers-retours","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11e","text":"Les retouches illimitées ne sont pas de la générosité, c’est une option non facturée que le client n’a pas demandée et dont il ne peut pas mesurer la valeur. Ce que nous écrivons à la place tient en quelques lignes :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11i","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11g","text":"Deux tours de retours consolidés par livrable.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k11h","text":" Consolidés veut dire un document du décideur nommé, pas cinq courriels de quatre personnes.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11l","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11j","text":"Un tour, c’est un ensemble de modifications à l’intérieur de la direction validée.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k11k","text":" Changer de direction n’est pas un tour, c’est un nouveau livrable, et nous le disons pendant la réunion plutôt que sur la facture.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11o","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11m","text":"Les tours supplémentaires sont chiffrés avant d’avoir lieu","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k11n","text":", à un tarif journalier annoncé, et n’arrivent jamais par surprise.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11r","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11p","text":"Un silence de plus de dix jours ouvrés clôt le tour.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k11q","text":" Pas comme une punition : parce qu’un projet en pause pendant un mois nous coûte le créneau que nous lui avions réservé.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11t","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11s","text":"C’est la quatrième ligne qui a fait le plus de travail. Les projets meurent rarement d’un désaccord, ils meurent de dérive, et la dérive coûte cher d’une façon que personne ne met sur une facture.[^taux]","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11v","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11u","text":"[^taux]: L’arithmétique qui m’a convaincue : un forfait de 9 000 livré en 70 heures donne un taux effectif d’environ 128 de l’heure. Le même projet, facturé 90 de l’heure, vaut 6 300 et réclame exactement la même compétence. Le forfait vous paie pour savoir faire, ce qui est la seule chose que le client achète vraiment.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11x","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11w","text":"---","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k11z","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k11y","text":"Les deux clauses qui ont sauvé le plus de projets","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k122","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k120","text":"La clause de date de contenu.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k121","text":" Les textes et les images sont dus à une date, cette date figure au planning avec un responsable nommé, et une date de contenu manquée décale la mise en ligne du même nombre de jours. Écrite, la clause paraît dure ; elle n’a jamais créé la moindre tension, parce qu’elle est acceptée en semaine zéro, quand tout le monde est optimiste et raisonnable. Sans elle, le studio absorbe le retard sans que ça se voie, immobilise l’équipe, puis se fait demander pourquoi le site est sorti en retard.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k125","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k123","text":"La clause de pause.","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k124","text":" Si un projet s’arrête plus de trois semaines pour des raisons côté client, le redémarrage coûte un montant annoncé, et le planning se renégocie au lieu de reprendre. Ce n’est pas une pénalité, c’est la description honnête de ce qui se passe : nous avons vendu ce temps à quelqu’un d’autre, le contexte doit être reconstruit, et la personne qui connaissait le mieux le code est maintenant à moitié engagée ailleurs. Nommer ce coût à l’avance transforme des excuses embarrassées en ligne de devis.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k127","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k126","text":"Aucune des deux clauses n’a jamais été brandie. Les deux ont changé des comportements, et c’est le travail d’une bonne clause : elle n’est pas là pour servir, elle est là pour être lue.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k129","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k128","text":"Quand l’heure reste la bonne réponse","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12b","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12a","text":"Un forfait suppose une chose ferme à chiffrer. Il existe trois cas où nous facturons encore du temps, et prétendre le contraire serait malhonnête : la maintenance courante, où le travail est réellement imprévisible et la relation longue ; le cadrage, où le livrable est la définition même du projet et ne peut pas être délimité avant d’exister ; et l’urgence, où le client veut quelqu’un de disponible plutôt que quelqu’un d’efficace. Dans ces trois cas, le client achète de la disponibilité ou de l’exploration, pas un résultat, et l’heure est la bonne unité pour les deux. L’erreur n’est pas la facturation horaire. L’erreur est de facturer à l’heure un projet dont vous connaissez déjà la forme, parce que vous facturez alors la chose la moins précieuse que vous apportez, votre temps, au lieu de la plus précieuse, à savoir que vous avez déjà fait cela onze fois et que vous savez lesquelles des quatre décisions vont compter.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12d","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12c","text":"Ce qu’on peut faire lundi","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12e","text":"Si vous ne changez qu’une chose, changez le nombre de chiffres. Prenez la prochaine proposition que vous alliez envoyer avec un prix unique, et coupez-la en une version plus petite que vous seriez content de livrer et une version plus grande dont vous seriez fier. Écrivez deux phrases sous chacune pour dire à qui elle convient. Envoyez les trois.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12h","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12g","text":"Le pire résultat possible, c’est que le client prenne la petite, et vous voilà avec un projet à un prix que vous avez fixé, dans un périmètre que vous avez écrit, qui se termine à une date que vous avez choisie. Ce n’est pas un mauvais lundi.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'pricing-a-redesign-without-guessing' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'the-real-cost-of-a-web-font' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « Ce que coûte vraiment une police web » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"k12j","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12i","text":"Un client nous a demandé le mois dernier s’il était possible d’ajouter une seconde police à son site. La licence était déjà payée : de son point de vue, c’était donc gratuit. L’hypothèse est légitime et elle est fausse, et l’explication a fini par devenir la note que j’aurais aimé qu’on me tende il y a dix ans.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12l","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12k","text":"Une police web se facture en quatre monnaies : des octets, des requêtes, un décalage de mise en page, et une décision de design que vous prendrez, que vous la remarquiez ou non.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12n","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12m","text":"Les octets, mesurés correctement","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k12p","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12o","text":"Commençons par le tableau des formats, parce que la moitié de la confusion vient de là.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t8m","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r8n","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12q","text":"Ce que vous servez","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12s","text":"Une graisse latine de labeur","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8q","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12u","text":"Bon à savoir","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r8r","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8s","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12w","text":"WOFF2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k12y","text":"18 à 26 Ko","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k130","text":"Compressé en Brotli, géré partout où ça compte","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r8v","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8w","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k132","text":"WOFF","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8x","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k134","text":"28 à 40 Ko","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c8y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k136","text":"Uniquement pour des navigateurs plus vieux que votre CMS","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r8z","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c90","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k138","text":"TTF ou OTF","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c91","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13a","text":"90 à 160 Ko","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c92","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13c","text":"Le fichier envoyé par la fonderie. Ne le servez jamais","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r93","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c94","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13e","text":"Variable, un axe, sous-ensemble latin","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c95","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13g","text":"35 à 60 Ko","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c96","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13i","text":"Le cas intéressant, voir plus bas","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13l","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13k","text":"Ce sont des fourchettes relevées sur nos propres builds, pas des chiffres de plaquette commerciale. Une romane à large jeu de caractères se place en haut de chaque fourchette, une linéale géométrique aux tables de crénage serrées en bas.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13n","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13m","text":"Le nombre qui compte n’est aucune ligne prise isolément. C’est le total, parce qu’une police bloque le rendu dans le seul sens qui importe : le texte l’attend ou bien il est remplacé en cours de route, et les deux se paient.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13p","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13o","text":"Une police variable n’est pas automatiquement moins chère","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13r","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13q","text":"C’est l’idée reçue que j’entends le plus souvent et elle mérite une réponse franche. Une police variable range toutes les graisses comprises entre ses extrêmes dans un seul fichier, plus les données d’interpolation qui permettent de circuler entre elles. Ce fichier est plus gros qu’une graisse statique et plus petit que cinq.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13t","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13s","text":"Le point de bascule se situe autour de trois :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13w","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13u","text":"Deux graisses","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k13v","text":" (romain, gras) : les deux fichiers statiques gagnent, en général de 15 à 20 Ko.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k13z","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k13x","text":"Trois graisses","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k13y","text":" : à peu près à égalité. Choisissez selon l’envie de garder de la souplesse plus tard.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k142","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k140","text":"Quatre graisses ou plus","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k141","text":", ou n’importe quel usage d’une graisse absente de la liste initiale : la variable gagne, et elle gagne de plus en plus à mesure que le design grandit.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k148","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k143","text":"Il existe un second argument en faveur de la variable, sans rapport avec le poids. Avec un axe de graisse, on peut poser ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k144","text":"font-weight: 560","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k145","text":" sur un titre et cesser de faire semblant que le design n’a jamais voulu que du demi-gras. Avec l’axe de taille optique (","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k146","text":"opsz","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k147","text":"), le caractère ajuste lui-même son contraste et son approche entre un texte de labeur à 14 px et un titre à 72 px, ce que le plomb faisait tout seul et que le numérique a mis trente ans à réapprendre.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14a","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k149","text":"Le sous-ensemble économise moins qu’espéré","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14e","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14b","text":"Faire un sous-ensemble, c’est ne livrer que les glyphes utiles. L’outil s’appelle ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14c","text":"fonttools","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14d","text":", et la commande n’a rien de spectaculaire :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k14f","language":"bash","code":"pyftsubset SourceSerif4-Variable.ttf \\\n  --output-file=source-serif-latin.woff2 \\\n  --flavor=woff2 \\\n  --layout-features=\"kern,liga,onum,tnum,frac\" \\\n  --unicodes=\"U+0000-00FF,U+0131,U+0152-0153,U+2000-206F,U+2122\""},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14p","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14g","text":"Deux avertissements tirés de l’expérience. D’abord, le gain est plus faible qu’annoncé pour un caractère purement latin, parce qu’un sous-ensemble latin représente déjà l’essentiel du fichier : les chiffres spectaculaires qu’on cite viennent du retrait du cyrillique et du grec d’une police paneuropéenne. Ensuite, attention à ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14h","text":"--layout-features","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14i","text":". Retirez ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14j","text":"kern","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14k","text":" et vos titres se désagrègent. Retirez ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14l","text":"liga","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14m","text":" et certaines polices perdent le ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14n","text":"fi","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k14o","text":" sur lequel vous comptiez. Et si le site est multilingue, souvenez-vous que le français réclame les guillemets chevrons et la ligature œ, tous deux hors de la plage ASCII, qui disparaissent sans bruit si vous découpez de mémoire plutôt que d’après le contenu réel.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14r","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14q","text":"Le bon réflexe consiste à déclarer aussi le sous-ensemble en CSS, pour que le navigateur puisse éviter un téléchargement inutile sur une page donnée :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k14s","language":"css","code":"@font-face {\n  font-family: \"Source Serif Var\";\n  src: url(\"/fonts/source-serif-latin.woff2\") format(\"woff2\");\n  font-weight: 200 900;\n  font-display: swap;\n  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+2000-206F, U+2122;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14u","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14t","text":"La police de secours que personne n’a dessinée","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14w","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14v","text":"Voici la partie coûteuse, et elle ne pèse pas un octet.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k14y","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14x","text":"<dl> <dt>FOIT, texte invisible</dt> <dd>Le navigateur masque le texte pendant le chargement de la police. Rien n’est lisible, la mise en page est stable, et le lecteur contemple une colonne vide. C’est ce que produit font-display: block.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k150","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k14z","text":"  <dt>FOUT, texte non stylé</dt> <dd>La police de secours s’affiche tout de suite, puis la police web la remplace. Lisible immédiatement, mais la page bouge au moment de la bascule. C’est font-display: swap.</dd>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k152","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k151","text":"  <dt>Décalage à la bascule</dt> <dd>Le coût mesurable du FOUT : la police de secours et la police web n’ont pas les mêmes métriques, donc les lignes se recomposent et tout ce qui suit saute. Cela atterrit dans le Cumulative Layout Shift, et c’est parfaitement évitable.</dd> </dl>","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k154","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k153","text":"Évitable, parce que le CSS sait forcer une police système à imiter les métriques de celle qui se télécharge encore :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k155","language":"css","code":"@font-face {\n  font-family: \"Source Serif fallback\";\n  src: local(\"Georgia\"), local(\"Times New Roman\");\n  size-adjust: 96.4%;\n  ascent-override: 98%;\n  descent-override: 24%;\n  line-gap-override: 0%;\n}\n\n:root {\n  --font-body: \"Source Serif Var\", \"Source Serif fallback\", Georgia, serif;\n}"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15c","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k157","_type":"link","href":"https://screenspan.net/fallback"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k156","text":"Ces quatre valeurs dépendent du couple de polices et ne se calculent pas à la main. Des outils comme ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k158","text":"Fallback Font Generator","marks":["k157"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k159","text":" ou le greffon ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15a","text":"fontaine","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15b","text":" mesurent les deux caractères et impriment la déclaration. Bien réglée, la bascule devient presque invisible : mêmes coupures de ligne, même hauteur de page, un simple changement de forme.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15g","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15d","text":"Si vous préférez ne pas mener ce combat, ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15e","text":"font-display: optional","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15f","text":" demande au navigateur de n’utiliser la police web que si elle est déjà en cache ou si elle arrive en une centaine de millisecondes, et de conserver la police de secours pour toute la visite sinon. Zéro décalage, garanti, au prix de quelques premiers visiteurs qui ne verront jamais votre caractère. Pour un site de texte avec un lectorat qui revient, l’échange est meilleur qu’il n’en a l’air.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15i","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15h","text":"Les requêtes, et la seule règle de préchargement","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15k","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15j","text":"Préchargez exactement les polices utilisées au-dessus de la ligne de flottaison, ce qui pour un site de texte veut dire une, éventuellement deux :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"code","_key":"k15l","language":"html","code":"<link rel=\"preload\" as=\"font\" type=\"font/woff2\"\n      href=\"/fonts/source-serif-latin.woff2\" crossorigin>"},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15p","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15m","text":"L’attribut ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15n","text":"crossorigin","marks":["code"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15o","text":" est obligatoire même pour un fichier servi depuis votre domaine, parce que les polices sont récupérées en mode CORS ; sans lui, le navigateur télécharge le fichier deux fois et vous avez aggravé la situation avec le sentiment d’avoir été malin. Précharger cinq polices est la même erreur à plus grande échelle : si tout est prioritaire, plus rien ne l’est.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15u","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k15r","_type":"link","href":"https://fontsource.org"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15q","text":"Hébergez vos polices vous-même. Un hébergeur tiers, c’est une résolution DNS, une poignée de main TLS et un second cache ; or les navigateurs cloisonnent leur cache HTTP par site depuis 2020, donc le vieil argument du cache partagé entre sites ne tient plus. ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15s","text":"Fontsource","marks":["k15r"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k15t","text":" empaquette les familles libres en modules npm, sous-ensembles déjà découpés.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15w","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15v","text":"Alors, combien coûte une seconde police ?","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k15y","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15x","text":"Pour ce client, honnêtement : environ 45 Ko, un préchargement supplémentaire que nous ne pouvions pas nous offrir, un couple de polices de secours à calibrer, et le risque d’une bascule visible sur la page à laquelle il tient le plus. Nous l’avons quand même livrée, financée par l’abandon d’une graisse qu’il n’utilisait pas. Toute la discipline est là. Rien n’est gratuit, tout se justifie si l’on connaît le prix, et la seule réponse inacceptable est de ne pas le connaître.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'the-real-cost-of-a-web-font' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
-- garde: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ec_posts WHERE slug = 'what-a-good-brief-looks-like' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0 | le tableau de l'article « À quoi ressemble un bon brief » (fr) s'affiche en tableau
UPDATE ec_posts SET content = '[{"_type":"block","_key":"k160","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k15z","text":"Cent six projets sont passés par ce studio. J’ai repris les onze qui ont perdu de l’argent et j’ai cherché le moment où ça a basculé. Dans neuf cas, ce moment se situait avant la réunion de lancement. Le brief ne contenait pas l’information dont le projet avait besoin, nous avons démarré quand même parce que le client était sympathique et le sujet amusant, et l’information manquante est revenue sous forme de périmètre en semaine sept.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k162","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k161","text":"Un brief n’est ni une liste de souhaits ni un cahier des charges technique. C’est le document le plus court qui rende une décision possible, et il doit répondre à quatre questions.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k164","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k163","text":"1. Qui décide","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k166","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k165","text":"Pas « qui est le client ». Qui, nommément, peut regarder une page et dire « oui, on met en ligne », sans demander à quelqu’un d’autre.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k168","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k167","text":"Si la réponse est un comité, le projet n’a pas de décideur, il a une file d’attente, et chaque tour de validation dure aussi longtemps que l’agenda le plus chargé du groupe.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k16a","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k169","text":"Si la réponse est un nom mais que cette personne n’a jamais assisté à une réunion avec nous, la réponse est fictive et se découvrira en semaine cinq.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k16c","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16b","text":"Si la réponse est « on décidera ensemble », l’intention est charmante et signifie que le premier vrai désaccord n’aura aucune procédure de résolution.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k16e","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16d","text":"Le remède est simple et il fonctionne : un décideur nommé, un rythme de validation convenu, et une règle écrite qui veut que les retours arrivent consolidés par cette personne plutôt qu’en cinq courriels séparés qui se contredisent. Nous le mettons dans le brief en une phrase, et nous la lisons à voix haute au lancement pour que personne ne tombe des nues plus tard.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k16g","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16f","text":"2. Ce qui existe déjà","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k16i","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16h","text":"La moitié de tout devis est en réalité une question d’inventaire. Un brief qui dit « refonte du site » décrit une quantité de travail inconnue ; un brief avec un inventaire décrit un projet.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"table","_key":"t97","hasHeaderRow":true,"rows":[{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r98","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c99","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16j","text":"Élément","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9a","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16l","text":"Qui le fournit","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9b","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16n","text":"Attendu pour","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9c","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16p","text":"S’il arrive en retard","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[],"isHeader":true}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r9d","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9e","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16r","text":"Textes définitifs, toutes pages","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9f","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16t","text":"Client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9g","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16v","text":"Semaine 3","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9h","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16x","text":"La mise en ligne recule, jour pour jour","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r9i","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9j","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k16z","text":"Photos et fichiers de logo","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9k","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k171","text":"Client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9l","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k173","text":"Semaine 2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9m","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k175","text":"On travaille sur des substituts, une reprise offerte","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r9n","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9o","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k177","text":"Charte graphique, s’il y en a une","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9p","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k179","text":"Client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9q","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17b","text":"Semaine 1","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9r","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17d","text":"On propose, le client valide en semaine 2","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r9s","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9t","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17f","text":"Accès analytics et DNS","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9u","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17h","text":"DSI du client","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9v","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17j","text":"Semaine 8","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9w","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17l","text":"La mise en ligne recule","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]},{"_type":"tableRow","_key":"r9x","cells":[{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9y","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17n","text":"Design, développement, déploiement","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"c9z","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17p","text":"Studio","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ca0","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17r","text":"Selon le planning","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]},{"_type":"tableCell","_key":"ca1","content":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17t","text":"C’est pour nous","marks":[]}],"markDefs":[]}]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k17w","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17v","text":"C’est la dernière colonne qui change les comportements. Pas comme une menace : elle est écrite dans la même phrase que notre propre pénalité, à savoir que tout ce qui figure sur notre ligne est notre problème et notre coût. Les gens acceptent une règle qui engage visiblement les deux parties, et un planning qui ne glisse que dans un sens n’est pas un planning, c’est un espoir.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k17y","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17x","text":"3. Ce qui vaut pour fini","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k180","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k17z","text":"« Fini » est le mot mal défini le plus cher de ce métier. Le nôtre est une liste que le client peut vérifier sans nous dans la pièce :","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k182","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k181","text":"Toutes les pages de l’arborescence convenue existent, avec leur contenu définitif, dans les deux langues.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k187","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[{"_key":"k184","_type":"link","href":"/fr/blog/a-performance-budget-that-survives-contact/"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k183","text":"Le site respecte le ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k185","text":"budget de performance","marks":["k184"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k186","text":" sur l’appareil de test convenu.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k189","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k188","text":"La navigation au clavier fonctionne de bout en bout, et le passage automatique d’accessibilité est propre sur tous les gabarits.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18b","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18a","text":"Mesure d’audience, redirections des anciennes URL et sitemap sont en ligne et vérifiés.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18d","style":"normal","listItem":"number","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18c","text":"L’équipe du client a suivi la prise en main du CMS et modifié une vraie page sans assistance.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18f","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18e","text":"Le point cinq vaut plus que les quatre autres. Un site que le client ne sait pas modifier est un site qui meurt en dix-huit mois, et c’est pendant la prise en main qu’on découvre que la personne qui va réellement le maintenir n’était présente à aucune réunion.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18h","style":"blockquote","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18g","text":"Un livrable que seul le studio peut vérifier n’est pas un livrable. C’est une promesse avec des étapes en plus.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18j","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18i","text":"4. Ce qui se passe en cas de désaccord","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18l","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18k","text":"Chaque projet en connaît un. En général la page d’accueil, en général en semaine six, en général parce que deux personnes voulaient des choses différentes et que les deux ont entendu oui.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18n","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18m","text":"Nous écrivons la procédure à l’avance, en trois lignes : le décideur tranche ; si la décision modifie le périmètre convenu, nous chiffrons le changement avant de le faire ; si le chiffrage est refusé, c’est la version validée précédemment qui part en ligne. C’est tout. Cela n’a jamais paru lourd dans la pratique, et les projets qui l’avaient sont ceux où personne n’a eu à hausser la voix.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18p","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18o","text":"Les trois questions qui révèlent un budget","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18r","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18q","text":"Les clients refusent souvent d’annoncer un chiffre, et la raison est recevable : ils pensent qu’il deviendra le prix. Nous posons donc trois questions qui produisent la même information sans faire perdre la face à personne.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18u","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18s","text":"« Que coûte une année de plus sans rien faire ? »","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k18t","text":" La réponse donne la taille du problème dans les unités du client, les seules qui comptent.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k18x","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18v","text":"« Avec quoi cet argent est-il en concurrence en interne ? »","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k18w","text":" S’il est en concurrence avec un recrutement, on parle de dizaines de milliers d’euros. S’il l’est avec un stand de salon, on parle de quelques milliers, et il faut le dire gentiment et vite.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k190","style":"normal","listItem":"bullet","level":1,"markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k18y","text":"« Combien a coûté la version précédente, et qu’est-ce qui s’est mal passé ? »","marks":["strong"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k18z","text":" On apprend l’ordre de grandeur et le traumatisme en même temps, et la seconde moitié est souvent plus utile que la première.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k192","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k191","text":"Trois réponses, aucun chiffre prononcé, et vous savez à un facteur deux près si la conversation mérite d’être poursuivie. C’est une gentillesse pour les deux parties : le pire résultat d’un premier rendez-vous n’est pas un projet perdu, c’est un projet accepté à un prix qui garantit la rancune en semaine neuf.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k194","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k193","text":"Le contenu est la date de livraison","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k196","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k195","text":"Si je ne pouvais mettre qu’une phrase en première page de chaque brief, ce serait celle-là, parce que c’est le meilleur indicateur d’un projet qui va prendre du retard et que presque personne ne s’en inquiète au départ : le design sera terminé bien avant les textes, le développement sera terminé avant les textes, le client aura sincèrement l’intention d’écrire les textes, puis la personne qui devait les écrire sera réquisitionnée par une urgence d’un autre service, et le site restera à quatre-vingt-quinze pour cent pendant six semaines pendant que tout le monde attend une page de copie que personne n’a eu le temps de rédiger, et au bout de ces six semaines quelqu’un proposera de lancer avec du texte provisoire, et c’est ainsi qu’un site part en ligne avec un titre « À propos » posé sur trois phrases tirées de la plaquette de 2019. Mettez les dates de contenu dans le brief, donnez-leur un responsable, et traitez une échéance de texte manquée exactement comme une échéance technique manquée.","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k198","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k197","text":"La page que nous renvoyons","marks":[]}]},{"_type":"block","_key":"k19d","style":"normal","markDefs":[{"_key":"k19a","_type":"link","href":"https://www.gov.uk/service-manual"}],"children":[{"_type":"span","_key":"k199","text":"Après un premier échange, nous envoyons une seule page : les quatre réponses telles que nous les avons comprises, le tableau d’inventaire, la définition du fini, et une fourchette de prix avec ce qui la fait monter ou descendre. Elle prend quarante minutes à écrire et ne s’est jamais révélée inutile. Soit le client la corrige, et c’est la correction la moins chère que le projet connaîtra jamais, soit il la signe, et nous démarrons un projet qui sait déjà ce qu’il est. Le ","marks":[]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k19b","text":"Service Manual de GOV.UK","marks":["k19a"]},{"_type":"span","_key":"k19c","text":" dit à peu près la même chose en beaucoup plus long, et il a raison depuis dix ans.","marks":[]}]}]', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')
  WHERE slug = 'what-a-good-brief-looks-like' AND locale = 'fr' AND instr(content, char(124, 32, 45, 45, 45, 32, 124)) > 0;
